    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日\n\n城下的坑道里，士兵等着炮火转向远处。雨雪打在白垩坡上。进攻向东展开，牵制当面的德军，接应即将到来的法军攻势。\n\n携弹队沿白垩路上行，担架从同一条路下来。坡脊之后传来机枪声，军士把各班的名字再念一遍，前队的回答被炮声盖住。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · Nine April nineteen seventeen\n\nMen wait in the tunnels beneath the town for the guns to lift. Sleet strikes the chalk slopes. The attack goes east to hold the German forces here ahead of the coming French offensive.\n\nAmmunition parties go up the chalk road; stretchers come down it. Machine guns answer beyond the crest. The NCO reads out the sections again, but the guns drown the reply from the leading infantry in front.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("一九一七年四月九日，英军在雨雪中向阿拉斯以东进攻，试图牵制德军，为即将开始的埃纳河法军攻势提供支援。白垩高地、洞穴和交通壕构成守军阵地，炮击之后仍有枪位继续射击。\n\n本连沿白垩路接近高地，坡脊遮住了后面的守军。残存壕道与枪位控制接近地段，英军携弹队和担架队也使用这条道路。战斗围绕坡面及其后方通路展开，前沿部队尚未接通所有邻段。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("On 9 April 1917, British forces attack east of Arras in rain and snow. The offensive is intended to draw German troops away from the coming French attack on the Aisne. Chalk heights, caves and communication trenches support the German defence, and some gun positions remain active after the bombardment.\n\nThe company advances along the chalk road towards the high ground. Surviving defenders behind the crest cover the approaches, while ammunition bearers and stretcher parties use the same road. The local fighting centres on these slopes and the passages linking the ridge to the rear.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n坑道兵在梯口摘下油灯，给最后一列人让路。靴底把白垩磨成细粉，墙上箭头指着出口。炮声停了一瞬，头顶落下的灰仍未停。\n\n他把松动的木撑敲回原位，身后又有人弯腰走来。出口外的雨雪打进灯罩，火苗缩在玻璃后面。地面上的口令传下来，梯上只剩沾泥的脚印。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe tunneller lifts his lamp from the ladder and lets the last file pass. Boots grind the chalk to powder. An arrow on the wall points towards daylight.\n\nHe knocks a loose prop back into place as more men stoop past him. Sleet reaches the lamp at the exit. An order comes down from above; muddy prints remain on the rungs.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月十二日\n\n厂墙缺口里有机枪开火，弹屑打在铁路堤下。炮击揭开了屋顶，地下掩体却还通着。投弹兵在壕角停下，把手榴弹逐个递向前队。\n\n步枪手伏在碎砖旁，观察两堵残墙之间的空地。携弹队背着箱子挤进交通壕，拐弯处的伤员向墙边让开。工厂里面又传来射击声。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · Twelve April nineteen seventeen\n\nA machine gun fires through a gap in the factory wall. Fragments strike below the railway bank. The roof has gone, but the underground shelters remain connected. Bombers halt at a traverse and pass grenades forward by hand.\n\nRiflemen watch the open space between two broken walls. The carrying party squeezes its boxes into the communication trench. A wounded man moves against the bricks to let them through. Firing starts again inside the works.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until sixteen May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("一九一七年四月十二日，阿拉斯以东的英军推进在勒厄遇到抵抗。化工厂、铁路堤和地下掩体相互支撑，炮击打碎厂墙，却未清除后面的全部枪位。双方仍在争夺外围接近壕。\n\n本连沿这些壕沟接近厂区。投弹兵进入短促壕角与残墙之间，步枪手照看相邻空地，携弹队沿狭窄通路跟进。厂内守军控制着附近道路，英军各队只能从破墙间观察前方，铁路堤仍遮住部分阵位。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("By 12 April 1917, the British advance east of Arras is encountering resistance around Roeux. The chemical works, railway embankment and underground shelters support one another. Bombardment has broken the factory walls without removing all the guns behind them, and the outer trenches remain contested.\n\nThe company is approaching through those trenches towards the factory outskirts. Bombing parties encounter short bends and broken masonry, while riflemen cover the open ground between them. Carrying parties follow along the confined approach. German positions in the works still threaten the roads needed by the British advance.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月12日\n\n修械兵把断了的枪托搁在厂房窗台上，碎玻璃随着射击声往下滑。他从帆布卷里取出螺丝刀，先擦净枪机上的砖粉。另一支步枪已递到手边。\n\n地下入口不断有人上来，他挪开工具给他们让路。墙外的机枪重新响起，窗框被打出一排新孔。他把修好的枪交还，窗台上又放下一只开裂的护木。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Roeux · 12 April 1917\n\nThe armourer lays a broken rifle stock on a factory sill. Gunfire shakes glass from the frame. He opens his tool roll and wipes brick dust from the bolt.\n\nMen keep climbing from the cellar, forcing him to move his tools. A machine gun starts beyond the wall. He hands back the repaired rifle; a split handguard takes its place.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n铁丝间留着四月战斗的残骸，新的进攻队又来到缺口前。白垩壕肩后冒出枪口，掩蔽部的出口还通着，投弹兵把枪榴弹送向壕角。\n\n前队已经越过障碍，携弹手的箱子却挂住了断丝。后面的人伏下帮他松开，邻段的射击忽近忽远。军士从弹坑里探头，寻找刚才出发的那一班。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nWreckage from April lies in the wire. Another assault party reaches the gap. A muzzle appears over the chalk parapet; the dugout exits are open. Rifle grenades fall towards the traverse while the leading men cross the obstacles.\n\nA bearer's box catches on a strand behind them. The next man lies down to free it. Firing rises and falls on the neighbouring sector. From a shell hole, the NCO searches for the section that has just gone forward.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("一九一七年五月三日，澳大利亚与英国部队再次进攻布勒库尔。四月战斗的残骸仍散在兴登堡线铁丝之间。障碍后，德军纵深壕和掩蔽部仍与后方连通，守军能在炮击之后重返胸墙。\n\n本连接近这片受损障碍，枪榴弹落向壕角，步兵从铁丝缺口向前。英军携弹队随后赶来，前沿壕沟的争夺影响着补给能否抵达已经越过障碍的人员。白垩壕肩与弹坑遮住部分动静，邻队的推进并不同时。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("On 3 May 1917, Australian and British troops renew the attack at Bullecourt. The April fighting has left wreckage among the Hindenburg Line's wire. Beyond it, deep German trenches and shelters remain connected to the rear, allowing defenders to return to the parapets after bombardment.\n\nThe company is approaching this damaged belt of obstacles. Rifle grenades reach the trench corners while infantry work through gaps in the wire. Ammunition bearers follow from the British side. The fighting around the forward trenches determines whether those carrying supplies can reach the men already beyond the obstacles.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n军邮兵把信袋压在胸前，沿白垩沟跟上前队。铁丝里挂着旧衣片，一封信从袋口滑出。他伏下捡回，封皮已被湿土抹去半个地址。\n\n壕角的士兵伸手接信，又缩回去握枪。军邮兵把余下的信袋塞进干处，等枪榴弹声过去。前方递来一只空背包，他翻过姓名牌，把它放到另一边。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe post orderly holds his bag against his chest and follows the chalk ditch. Old cloth hangs in the wire. A letter slips out; wet earth covers half the address.\n\nA man reaches from a traverse, then takes his rifle again. The orderly puts the letters somewhere dry and waits through the rifle-grenade fire. An empty pack arrives from ahead; he turns over its name tag.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月七日\n\n地面猛然抬起，山脊的旧壕道没入烟尘。普卢默的第二集团军向前推进，澳新部队在邻段出发。军士循着刚露出的坑岸，寻找通往高处的路。\n\n枪组把枪架拖过松土，携弹手试着踩出一条硬路。原先标定的地形已经改变，担架队在后面停住，等前队报回尚能通行的缺口。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer's Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("一九一七年六月七日破晓前，梅西讷山脊下的地雷爆炸。普卢默的第二集团军按炮兵计划进攻，澳大利亚与新西兰部队也在邻段行动。爆破摧毁壕沟，在接近路上留下陡峭坑岸。\n\n本连随炮火进入破碎地面，步枪手穿行弹坑之间，机枪组把器材带向坑岸。瓦砾中仍有幸存德军哨位，携弹队和担架队从后方跟进。作战准备时标明的小路已有变化，松土和断坡限制部队之间的观察。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("Before dawn on 7 June 1917, mines explode beneath the German positions on Messines ridge. Plumer's Second Army attacks under a prepared artillery plan, with Australian and New Zealand formations on adjoining sectors. The explosions have destroyed trenches and left steep crater banks across the approaches.\n\nThe company advances into this broken ground behind the bombardment. Riflemen pass between craters while machine gun crews bring their equipment towards the banks. Surviving German posts remain among the debris. Ammunition and stretcher parties follow through passages that have changed since the attack was prepared.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe ground rises and the old ridge trenches vanish into dust. Plumer’s Second Army advances; Australian and New Zealand troops move on the adjoining sectors. The NCO follows the fresh crater lip, looking for a passage onto the heights.\n\nThe gun crew drags its mounting over loose earth. A bearer tests each step for firm ground. The landmarks on the sketch have gone. Behind them, the stretcher party waits for word of a gap that will carry a loaded stretcher.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n测绘员把图板支在新坑岸上，旧图里的树和壕角已对不上。他擦掉一条线，从露出的白垩层重新量起。炮兵联络官站在旁边，铅笔还悬在纸上。\n\n皮尺从松土上拖过，读数的人几次滑到坑底。测绘员把新路画在旧壕旁，留下通向脊顶的箭头。枪架沿那条路抬过去，靴底把纸边踩进了泥里。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe surveyor sets his board on a fresh crater lip. Trees and trench corners no longer match his sheet. He rubs out a line and measures from the exposed chalk.\n\nThe tape drags over loose earth; the reader keeps slipping downhill. A new path goes onto the sheet beside the old trench. A gun mounting passes that way, and a boot presses the paper edge into the mud.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions at the opening of the Messines attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月九日\n\n新胸墙还缺着一角，枪组已把枪口转向东坡。进攻过去两日，阵地上的铁锹没有停过。换防队循弹坑间的小路上来，先问哪一道壕沟还能走。\n\n预备队在脊后集合，携弹手从伤员身旁挤过。德军在对面坡下活动，军士伏在新垒的土袋间观察。壕底还有旧枪架留下的凹痕。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · Nine June nineteen seventeen\n\nA corner is missing from the new parapet. The gun already faces the eastern slope. Two days have passed since the attack, and spades are still at work. Reliefs follow the crater path and ask which trench remains open.\n\nReserves gather behind the crest. Bearers edge past the wounded with their ammunition. German parties move below the opposite slope. The NCO watches through the fresh sandbags; the floor still bears the marks of the former gun mounting.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("梅西讷进攻过去两日，英军仍在加固山脊上的新前线。枪位转向德军后方，胸墙正在修补，坑岸小路输送弹药与换防人员。东面坡后的德军已开始集结反击队。\n\n本连守着新占阵地的一段，更广地段还有英军和澳新部队。枪组照看接近线，预备队在山脊后集合。受损道路同时承担前送补给与后送伤员，尚未完成的土工使部分阵位暴露。新旧壕道的朝向不同，部队联络仍在调整。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("Two days after the attack at Messines, the British front on the ridge is still being consolidated. Gun positions face towards the German rear, breastworks are being repaired, and crater paths carry ammunition and reliefs. German counterattack parties are gathering on the eastern slopes.\n\nThe company is holding part of this newly occupied line alongside British, Australian and New Zealand troops in the wider sector. Its guns cover the approaches while reserves assemble behind the ridge. The damaged paths support both forward supply and evacuation, with unfinished earthworks leaving parts of the position exposed to renewed attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月9日\n\n木工从毁坏掩体里拖出一根还可用的横梁，锯口里全是砂土。他用钉拔把弯钉取下，钉在新胸墙后面。山脊另一侧又有炮弹落下。\n\n换防队从窄处经过，他把半锯的木料竖到墙边。新枪位缺一块踏板，旧门板便被截成两段。机枪转向东坡时，他蹲在下面把最后一枚钉子敲平。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Messines Ridge · 9 June 1917\n\nThe carpenter drags a usable beam from a ruined dugout. Grit fills the saw cut. He pulls out bent nails and drives them into the new parapet supports.\n\nReliefs pass the narrow opening, so he stands his timber against the wall. A missing step is cut from an old door. When the gun turns towards the eastern slope, he flattens the last nail beneath it.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日\n\n木板路在积水中断开，前队停在最后一块木板上。城外的排水沟已经被炮火打坏，弹坑连成水面。远处德军枪位开火，水上浮着新溅起的泥。\n\n壕炮组带着器材赶来，野炮还堵在后面的路上。携弹手把箱子举过水面，伤员坐在路边等待。军士试过脚下的硬地，才让下一人跨出。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · Thirty-one July nineteen seventeen\n\nThe duckboards end in standing water. The leading men stop on the last plank. Shellfire has broken the drains outside the town and joined the craters into pools. A German gun opens beyond them; fresh mud splashes onto the surface.\n\nThe mortar crew brings its equipment forward. Field guns are caught on the road behind. Bearers lift their boxes above the water, passing wounded men seated beside the path. The NCO tests the ground before the next man steps off.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("一九一七年七月三十一日，第三次伊普尔战役的皮尔克姆进攻展开。炮火破坏城外排水系统，雨水漫进田野和旧弹坑，德军哨位仍散在积水接近地段。少数干路承载着前线交通。\n\n本连沿尚存硬地和木板路行动。壕炮已经赶到前沿，野炮与补给仍受后方道路阻碍。携弹队和伤员共用少数通路，积水与受损壕沟分开前进部队，也限制着对邻军和德军枪位的观察。炮击还在不断改变道路状况。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("The attack towards Pilckem opens on 31 July 1917 as part of the Third Battle of Ypres. Shellfire has damaged the drainage around the city, and rain is filling fields and old craters. German posts remain scattered across the flooded approaches.\n\nThe company's sector follows the surviving firm ground and duckboard paths. Trench mortars have come forward while field batteries and supplies struggle on the roads behind. Ammunition bearers and wounded men share the few usable passages. Water and damaged trenches separate the advancing parties, limiting observation of neighbouring positions and the surviving German guns.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n驭手拉住缰绳，骡子的前蹄已陷过木板边缘。炮弹箱在驮架上向一侧倾斜，他割断结绳，让后面的人逐只接走。积水里浮着刚折断的木片。\n\n空驮架减轻了重量，骡子仍不肯迈出那一步。驭手摸到颈下，把绳子绕过硬桩慢慢牵回。路上让出一点空处，后一匹骡子又低头闻了闻水面。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe driver checks the reins as a mule steps off the duckboards. Its load tips sideways. He cuts the lashings so men behind can take the boxes one at a time.\n\nThe empty pack is lighter, but the mule will not move. He leads it back slowly with a rope around a firm post. The track clears a little; the next animal lowers its muzzle towards the water.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月十六日\n\n农舍只剩一面墙，墙后的混凝土掩体仍在射击。前队沿湿田接近，邻队的钢盔隔着积水时隐时现。观察员伏在碎砖上，辨认射孔的位置。\n\n迫击炮弹由后方传来，一箱接着一箱。通往农场的硬路很窄，担架队已在路边停下。军士把手举过残墙，让失去联系的步枪手看见。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · Sixteen August nineteen seventeen\n\nOne wall remains of the farmhouse. A concrete shelter behind it is still firing. Men approach across the wet field; helmets on the next sector appear and disappear beyond the pools. The observer lies on broken bricks, searching for the loophole.\n\nMortar ammunition arrives from the rear, box after box. The firm track to the farm is narrow. A stretcher party has stopped beside it. The NCO raises a hand over the wall for riflemen who have lost contact.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("一九一七年八月十六日，英军在朗厄马尔克穿过湿田进攻。农场废墟与混凝土掩体散布其间，德军据点隔着剩余干路相互支撑。邻近部队各自接近不同阵位，积水和破碎地面打断彼此联系。\n\n本连接近农场残墙，迫击炮弹从后方运来，观察员辨认仍有人据守的掩体。少数硬路同时运送补给和伤员，分散阵位之间难以通行。控制干路的德军枪位能够威胁多个接近方向，英军各队受到不同程度的阻挡。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("The British attack at Langemarck on 16 August 1917 advances through wet fields containing farm ruins and concrete shelters. German strongpoints cover one another across the remaining dry approaches. Neighbouring formations are moving towards separate positions, with water and broken ground interrupting their contact.\n\nThe company approaches the ruined farms while mortar ammunition comes forward from the rear. Observers are identifying occupied shelters among the masonry. The few firm tracks also carry supplies and casualties, making movement between the scattered positions difficult. German guns on those tracks can threaten troops advancing towards more than one farm.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月16日\n\n摄影兵在农舍残墙后架起相机，地脚陷进一只旧弹坑。他把镜头朝向混凝土射孔，等烟从墙前散开。快门布上沾着雨水，手指一直扶在边缘。\n\n一个小队沿窄路经过，相机前只留下摇动的草茎。他收起三脚架，从碎砖间换到另一处墙角。掩体再次开火，取景框里便只剩压低的钢盔。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Langemarck · 16 August 1917\n\nThe photographer sets his camera behind a farm wall. A tripod foot sinks into an old crater. He points towards the concrete loophole and waits for the smoke to clear.\n\nA section passes on the narrow track, leaving grass moving in the frame. He carries the tripod to another corner among the bricks. The shelter fires again; helmets disappear below the edge of the view.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月二十日\n\n树桩之间落着刚翻起的土，炮火正向林地深处移动。前队越过一道浅脊，邻班便从视野中消失。枪组停下来，把枪架放在残根之间。\n\n携弹队还带着铁锹，新占的地段来不及挖深。德军哨位在断木后射击，后面的道路又有增援上来。步枪手把枯枝拨开，枪口朝着林缘。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · Twenty September nineteen seventeen\n\nFresh earth falls between the stumps as the barrage moves deeper into the wood. The leading men cross a low ridge and lose sight of the next section. The gun crew sets its mounting among the exposed roots.\n\nBearers bring spades with the ammunition. There has been little time to deepen the captured position. German posts fire from behind broken timber. More men arrive along the crowded track. A rifleman pushes dead branches aside and points his muzzle towards the tree line.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("一九一七年九月二十日，英军在梅宁路以集中炮火支援有限推进。路旁树林只剩树桩和断路，德军预备队仍在前沿之后，准备反击林缘失去的地段。残存坡脊分割着双方视野。\n\n本连进入受损林地，枪组跟进朝向德军接近线的位置，携弹队运来弹药和工具。树桩与地形遮住邻军动静。眼前地段既有幸存德军哨位，也有正在组织防御的新占土地。道路拥挤，前送人员与后送伤员从相同通路经过。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("On 20 September 1917, the British attack along the Menin Road uses concentrated artillery support for a limited advance. The woods beside the road have been reduced to stumps and broken paths. German reserves remain behind the forward positions, ready to counterattack ground lost near the tree line.\n\nThe company advances through this damaged woodland. Gun crews follow towards positions facing the German approaches, while carrying parties bring ammunition and tools. Ridges and tree remnants interrupt observation between neighbouring units. The immediate sector contains both surviving German posts and newly occupied ground still being organised for defence.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月20日\n\n炮兵联络兵把新地图摊在树桩上，手指沿弹幕线往前移。林地深处的爆炸还在继续，步兵已经越过浅脊。电话受话器里传来一句话，他把它写到湿纸边上。\n\n线从残根间穿过，一处被靴跟扯紧。联络兵弯腰放松线圈，把受话器交给身旁的人。新占的枪位开始挖土，他在图上给那一角添了一个小方框。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Menin Road · 20 September 1917\n\nThe liaison runner spreads a new map on a stump. His finger follows the barrage line. Explosions continue deeper in the wood while infantry cross the low ridge.\n\nA boot pulls the telephone wire tight among the roots. He releases another coil and hands over the receiver. Men start digging at the captured gun post; a small square is added to his map.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 一九一七年十一月二十日\n\n履带压进坚实田地，铁丝在战车前面倒下。步兵跟着Mark IV来到壕边，壕底的转角却还在射击。炮声盖过发动机，前车已越过下一道障碍。\n\n步枪手伏在履带留下的沟里，投弹兵向掩蔽部接近。携弹队从缺口进入，先来的人员指着深壕让他们绕行。战车的背影逐渐被坡脊遮住。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · Twenty November nineteen seventeen\n\nTracks bite into firm ground and wire falls before the tanks. Infantry follow a Mark IV to the trench, but a bend below is still firing. The guns drown the engine. The leading tank has crossed another obstacle.\n\nRiflemen lie in the track marks while bombers approach a dugout. Bearers enter through the gap with their boxes. Men already across point out the deep trench and direct them around it. The tank disappears behind the next rise.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("一九一七年十一月二十日，英军在康布雷附近以大量坦克进攻兴登堡线。坚实田地承住Mark IV履带，铁丝后的德军深壕保护着通往重要公路和铁路枢纽的路线。炮兵支援初次推进。\n\n本连跟在坦克之后越过受损障碍。装甲经过的壕角和掩蔽部里仍有守军，第一道防线后面的道路输送双方弹药与增援。壕沟内的争夺影响着后续英军能走哪些接近路，坦克与步兵的进度并不完全一致。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("On 20 November 1917, British forces attack the Hindenburg Line near Cambrai with massed tanks. Firm fields allow Mark IVs to approach the wire, beyond which deep German trenches protect the routes to a major road and railway centre. Artillery supports the opening advance.\n\nThe company follows the tanks through the damaged obstacles. German defenders remain in trench bends and shelters passed by the armour. Roads beyond the first line carry ammunition and reinforcements for both sides. Infantry fighting in these trenches determines which approaches the following British troops and their supplies can use.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷 · 1917年11月20日\n\n驾驶员隔着狭缝看见铁丝倒下，履带咬住干硬的土。车里有人拍了两下隔板，炮组开始转动炮尾。发动机震得水壶碰响，外面的步兵时隐时现。\n\n深壕来到车头下，他压住操纵杆，等车身越过断边。侧舷传来急促敲击，驾驶员把车速放慢。视缝里重新出现道路，路边一只钢盔指向仍在射击的壕角。\n\n英军在康布雷集中使用坦克突破兴登堡防线。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai · 20 November 1917\n\nThrough his slit, the driver sees wire fall beneath the tracks. Firm earth holds the tank. Two knocks sound on the partition and the gun crew shifts its breech.\n\nA deep trench comes under the nose; he holds the controls until the hull crosses its edge. Sharp knocks sound against the side. He slows down as a helmet beside the road points towards a firing traverse.\n\nBritain massed tanks against the Hindenburg Line at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日\n\n林口的机枪转了方向，弹带横过刚堆好的土袋。德军反击正在逼近，换防人员和携弹队还往林中走。撤下来的伤员在路口迎面遇见他们。\n\n断树后传来步枪声，浅洼遮住侧翼的动静。军士把返回的人引进交通壕，再让前送的队伍通过。担架的木柄擦过壕壁，刮下一层湿土。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · Thirty November nineteen seventeen\n\nThe gun at the woodland exit changes direction. Its belt crosses newly stacked sandbags. German counterattacks are closing in while reliefs and ammunition parties still enter the wood. Wounded men meet them at the junction.\n\nRifle fire comes from behind broken trees. A hollow conceals the flank. The NCO guides returning men into the communication trench, then lets the carrying party through. A stretcher handle scrapes wet earth from the wall; the bearers turn it carefully at the bend.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("一九一七年十一月三十日，德军反击压向康布雷附近的英军突出部。布尔隆林旁道路仍前送弹药与换防人员，伤员和撤回部队则向后行进。新的德军接近方向威胁此前位于英军后方的通路。\n\n本连位于林缘出口及其交通壕附近，机枪转向反击方向，照看拥挤道路。断树和浅洼藏着侧翼移动，出口沿线的步兵战斗影响着突出部撤出人员的通行。前行与返回队伍仍在使用同一批狭窄路线。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("German counterattacks on 30 November 1917 are pressing the British salient near Cambrai. At Bourlon Wood, roads carry ammunition and reliefs towards the front while wounded and withdrawing parties move back. New German approaches threaten routes that lay behind the earlier British advance.\n\nThe company is positioned near the woodland exit and its communication trenches. Machine guns are turning towards the counterattack, covering roads crowded with traffic. Broken trees and shallow hollows conceal movement on the flanks. Infantry fighting along the exit affects the passage of troops still coming out of the salient.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n军医在林口废屋里铺开器械，门板上落着树皮和尘土。刚送来的人握着一截断带，另一只手仍在发抖。他把水倒进搪瓷盆，盆底很快看不清了。\n\n外面的枪位换了方向，门口的人便把桌子推向墙边。军医剪开湿透的袖口，让助手换上干布。下一名伤员停在门外，靴上的泥沿台阶慢慢落下。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe medical officer opens his instruments in a ruined house at the wood edge. Bark and dust cover the door. A newly arrived man grips a broken strap with a shaking hand.\n\nThe gun outside changes direction, and the table is pushed against the wall. He cuts a wet sleeve open and asks for dry cloth. Another casualty waits outside; mud falls slowly from his boots onto the step.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月\n\n哨位没有回答，值更军士又听了一会儿。铁丝前的低地留着脚印，零星枪声从德军阵地方向传来。轻装巡逻队走进湿沟，后面的人掩住灯光。\n\n前哨与连部之间有几段断线，尚无人带回消息。留守的哨兵望着沟口，换防队已在壕内等候。泥水里响了一下，枪手把手放到扳机旁。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February nineteen eighteen\n\nThe post gives no answer. The duty NCO listens again. Footprints mark the low ground before the wire; scattered shots come from the German line. A light patrol enters the wet ditch, and the man behind covers the lamp.\n\nWire is broken between the outpost and headquarters. No runner has returned. Sentries watch the mouth of the ditch while the relief waits in the trench. Something stirs in the water. A gunner rests his hand beside the trigger.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("一九一八年二月，康布雷前线在此前秋季战斗后继续修壕、换防和巡逻。雨雪在铁丝前的低地留下脚印，前哨观察德军阵位是否有变化，零星枪声打断冬季地段的安静。\n\n本连夜间派轻装巡逻队接近前哨。湿沟和相邻交通壕限制视野与行动，一处哨位没有回答，可能与通信损坏有关，也可能有敌军活动。英军哨兵继续留在阵线上，巡逻队查看前方地面，留下的人员等待他们带回情况。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("In February 1918, the Cambrai front remains occupied by trench repairs, reliefs and patrols after the previous autumn's battles. Rain and snow leave tracks in the low ground before the wire. Outposts watch for changes in the German positions, with intermittent firing breaking the quiet of the winter sector.\n\nThe company sends a light patrol towards the forward approaches at night. Wet ditches and nearby communication trenches limit visibility and movement. A missing reply from an outpost may reflect damaged communications or enemy activity. Sentries remain along the British line while the patrol checks the ground ahead.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n巡逻领队用布包住水壶，把松动的扣环一个个摸紧。雪地里先前的脚印已冻成硬边，他沿着旧沟口试走一段。身后的人只用手势问路。\n\n壕外的铁丝没有声音，远处偶尔亮起一道照明弹。他带人伏到洼地里，等白光移过去。返回点挂着一片暗布，风把它贴在支柱上，又轻轻掀开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe patrol leader wraps his water bottle and tightens loose buckles by touch. Earlier footprints have frozen hard. He tests the old ditch while the men behind ask their way with gestures.\n\nThe wire is silent; a flare rises in the distance. He brings the patrol into a hollow and waits for the light to pass. A dark cloth marks the return point, lifting briefly from its post in the wind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日\n\n路口挤满第五集团军撤下来的人员，有人扶着伤员，有人找自己的军士。炮火打断了电话线，浓雾中的前哨已无回音。德军从支点之间穿过，枪声移向后方。\n\n后卫枪组守在道路旁，等最后一批失散人员经过。携弹手把箱子留在枪位，转身接过一副担架。军士查完眼前的人数，又向雾里望去。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · Twenty-one March nineteen eighteen\n\nFifth Army men coming back crowd the junction. Some support wounded comrades; others ask for their NCO. Shellfire has cut the telephone wire. The posts in the fog give no answer, and German parties are passing between the strongpoints.\n\nThe rearguard gun waits beside the road for the last scattered men. A bearer leaves his ammunition at the position and takes a stretcher handle. The NCO counts those beside him, then looks into the fog again. Firing comes from farther behind.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("一九一八年三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势在浓雾和猛烈炮击中压向英军前线。第五集团军守着宽阔地段，德军突击队从幸存支点之间穿过。电话交换所和道路交叉口遭到炮击，前沿报告难以送达。\n\n本连担任受威胁道路上的后卫，接应从这一地段返回的孤立部队，其中有伤员，也有与本队失散的士兵。德军沿缺口深入，威胁着受损阵位后方的联络，英军正沿剩余通路重新集结。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("On 21 March 1918, Operation Michael opens against the British front in dense fog and heavy bombardment. The Fifth Army holds a wide sector, where German assault parties are passing between surviving strongpoints. Telephone exchanges and road junctions are under fire, disrupting reports from the forward line.\n\nThe company serves as a rear guard along a road threatened by the advance. Isolated British parties are returning through the sector, including wounded men and troops separated from their units. German movement through the gaps threatens the communications needed to regroup behind the damaged positions.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n接线员把耳机按紧，交换机上的插孔接连失去声音。圣康坦方向的炮火没有间断，一条线里只听见拖动电话的杂响。他拔出插头，换到备用线上。\n\n撤下来的军官在桌边报出新地址，接线员把旧牌翻过来。图上的道路还在，通话的人却已换了位置。门外有人卷起线盘，他把仍能接通的那根留下。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe operator presses his headset close as sockets fall silent on the switchboard. The guns towards St Quentin keep firing. One line carries only the sound of a telephone being dragged.\n\nAn officer arriving from the front gives a new address. The operator turns the old label over; the roads remain on the map, but the callers have moved. Outside, men gather cable, leaving the one line that still answers.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 一九一八年四月九日\n\n联络兵带来邻段失守的消息，电话里却无人回答。河沟把田野分成窄块，机枪声沿水面传来。侧翼的步枪手离开旧枪位，向路口的零散哨兵靠拢。\n\n渡口旁有队伍重新集合，携弹队也要从这里经过。军士用地图核对前哨，把一名传令兵留在路边。对岸的枪还在响，名册上几个阵位没有回报。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · Nine April nineteen eighteen\n\nA runner brings word of a breach on the neighbouring sector. The telephone is silent. Ditches divide the fields, carrying the sound of machine guns across the water. Riflemen leave their old position to join scattered sentries at the junction.\n\nTroops gather beside the crossing. The carrying party needs that road too. The NCO checks the posts against his map and leaves a runner beside the track. Guns still fire across the bank. Several marked positions have sent no report.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("一九一八年四月九日，德军乔治特攻势在利斯河低地开始。葡萄牙与英军阵位受到攻击，邻段被突破的报告传到英军后方。河沟分开田野，弹药交通依赖少数道路。\n\n本连沿受威胁侧翼移动，接起道路交叉口附近的分散哨位。电话线中断，邻近阵位情况不明。德军分队穿过低地，英军在尚可使用的渡口和公路附近重新组织，携弹队也需要从这些路线靠近前沿，河岸两侧仍有阵位抵抗。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("The German Georgette offensive begins on 9 April 1918 in the Lys lowlands. Portuguese and British positions are under attack, and reports of a breach in the neighbouring sector reach the British rear. River ditches divide the fields, leaving ammunition traffic dependent on a few roads.\n\nThe company moves along the threatened flank to reconnect scattered posts near a road junction. Telephone lines are interrupted, and the condition of neighbouring positions is uncertain. German parties are advancing through the low ground while British troops reorganise around the crossings and roads still available to them.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n钉掌兵抬起马的后蹄，从铁掌里剔出一块尖石。炮车在利斯河沟边等候，驭手握着缰绳看向路口。刚砸直的铁钉还带着炉灰。\n\n渡口又送来一匹跛马，他把工具箱挪到篱笆后。水从马腹下滴到皮围裙上，车轮已经深陷泥槽。他钉牢松开的掌边，挥手让炮车先往硬路上走。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe farrier lifts a hind hoof and prises a sharp stone from the shoe. A gun wagon waits beside a Lys ditch. Its driver watches the junction with the reins in his hands.\n\nA lame horse comes from the crossing, so the tools move behind a hedge. Water drips onto the leather apron; wagon wheels are deep in the ruts. He secures the loose shoe and sends the team towards firm ground.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日\n\n果园外传来履带声，村里的路口已经被德军占据。英军战车从残墙旁转出，步兵贴着沟边跟上。车组看不见墙后的动静，枪声却从巷口传来。\n\n通往亚眠的路仍在身后，携弹队停在倒塌的院门前。军士指了指侧面的缺口，让步枪手分头进去。入夜反击的准备还在继续，眼前的街道尚未安静。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen\n\nTracks sound beyond the orchard. German troops hold the village junction. A British tank turns beside a broken wall and infantry follow the ditch. Its crew cannot see behind the masonry, where firing comes from a lane.\n\nThe road to Amiens lies behind them. Bearers stop at a fallen gate. The NCO points riflemen towards a gap in the side wall. Preparations continue for the counterattack after dark, but the street ahead is still under fire from the ruins.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("一九一八年四月二十四日，德军步兵和坦克进攻亚眠接近路上的维莱布勒托讷。英军装甲在村外迎战，断墙、果园和路口遮断车辆与步兵之间的视野。澳大利亚部队准备入夜反击。\n\n本连在通向亚眠的道路周围交战。德军已进入村庄，英军仍留在接近地段。车组只能从车内看见部分地面，步枪手在废墟与小巷遇到守军。村道把这些分散部队与后方相连，墙后的阵位仍难以直接观察。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("On 24 April 1918, German infantry and tanks attack Villers-Bretonneux on the approaches to Amiens. British armour engages near the village outskirts. Broken walls, orchards and road junctions interrupt views between the vehicles and the infantry, while Australian troops prepare for a counterattack after dark.\n\nThe company is fighting around the routes leading towards Amiens. German troops have entered the village, and British parties remain on its approaches. Tank crews see only parts of the ground from their vehicles; riflemen encounter defenders among the ruins and lanes. The village roads connect these separated groups with their rear.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n炮手靠在炮尾旁，从视孔里找村口的车影。车身一停，他便把瞄准线挪过残墙。射击后涌进来的烟遮住了炮闩，他用手摸到下一发弹药。\n\n驾驶员把战车退回一点，果园又回到视孔前。车外有人指向一条小巷，车组只能逐次转动车身。另一声炮响从墙后传来，空弹壳滚到炮手的靴边。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe gunner braces beside the breech and searches for a tank at the village entrance. As the hull stops, he shifts his sight past a broken wall. Smoke hides the breech after firing.\n\nThe driver draws back slightly, bringing the orchard into view again. A man outside points towards an alley; the crew turns the hull by degrees. A gun answers beyond the wall, and an empty case rolls against the gunner's boot.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日\n\n低雾遮住村界，战车从前队身旁驶过。澳大利亚与加拿大部队已经出发，炮火向远处延伸。步枪手越过田埂，隔着雾寻找相邻队伍的身影。\n\n传令兵在岔路留下指路的人，携弹队沿车辙跟来。孤立枪位还在抵抗，前面时而有人停下卧倒。发动机的声音渐远，一辆战车只剩露出雾面的车顶。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · Eight August nineteen eighteen\n\nLow mist hides the village boundary. A tank passes the leading infantry. Australian and Canadian troops are moving forward as the barrage lifts into the distance. Riflemen cross the field bank and search through the mist for the next party.\n\nA runner leaves a man at the fork to guide the bearers following the tracks. Isolated posts still resist. Men ahead stop and lie down when shots reach them. Engine noise fades until only a tank's roof shows above the mist.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("一九一八年八月八日清晨，协约国在低雾中进攻亚眠以东。澳大利亚与加拿大部队推进，英军位于北侧，法军在更南一侧。炮兵、坦克和飞机共同支援，打击德军前沿及增援交通。\n\n本连随初次炮火穿过田野与受损村界，步兵越过孤立哨位，坦克沿接近路继续移动。携弹队从道路跟进，传令兵维持邻队联系。雾和幸存德军阵位仍遮断视野，各支部队无法直接看清整段推进前线。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("At dawn on 8 August 1918, Allied forces attack east of Amiens under low mist. Australian and Canadian formations advance with British troops to the north and French troops farther south. Artillery, tanks and aircraft support the operation together, disrupting the German forward positions and reinforcements.\n\nThe company moves through fields and damaged village boundaries behind the opening fire. Infantry pass isolated posts while tanks continue along the approaches. Ammunition parties follow the roads, and runners maintain contact between neighbouring units. Mist and surviving German positions still interrupt observation across the advancing front.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n气象观察员用袖口擦去表盘上的雾，把风旗递给身旁的人。亚眠以东的田野传来发动机声，近处的篱笆还看不清。纸上的记录被水珠洇开一角。\n\n他把风旗举过低墙，布条先垂下，又慢慢偏向一边。前队已经出发，电话催来新的读数。旗杆收回墙后时，雾里出现了履带压过草地的声音。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe weather observer wipes mist from a dial and passes over the wind pennant. Engines sound in the fields east of Amiens. Even the nearest hedge is difficult to see.\n\nHe raises the pennant above a low wall; the cloth hangs, then turns slowly aside. The leading troops have gone and the telephone asks for another reading. As he lowers the pole, tracks can be heard crossing grass in the fog.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · 26 August 1918\n\nThe cook holds a lid down as hot soup splashes over the cart. A gun wagon passes the junction towards the Scarpe. His cart jolts after it, the loose catch wrapped in sacking.\n\nOnly a patch of dry ground remains at the new position. He sets the food against a broken wall as men bring enamel mugs, still looking forward. When the bottom of the pot shows, another party arrives outside.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月二十六日\n\n工兵在旧铁丝旁蹲下，刚翻出的炮弹还半埋在土里。加拿大部队从前方阵位经过，村边德军后卫继续射击。白垩田地上，新弹坑叠着旧弹坑。\n\n携弹队等在障碍缺口，前队沿工兵标出的通路向前。步枪手在田界卧倒，担架从他们身后送回。军士拦住一名抄近路的士兵，指向那枚露出的弹体。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · 26 August 1918\n\nThe cook holds a lid down as hot soup splashes over the cart. A gun wagon passes the junction towards the Scarpe. His cart jolts after it, the loose catch wrapped in sacking.\n\nOnly a patch of dry ground remains at the new position. He sets the food against a broken wall as men bring enamel mugs, still looking forward. When the bottom of the pot shows, another party arrives outside.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · Twenty-six August nineteen eighteen\n\nA sapper crouches beside the old wire. A shell newly exposed by the bombardment lies half buried. Canadian troops pass the forward positions while German rearguards fire from the village edge. Fresh craters overlap the older ones in the chalk.\n\nBearers wait at the gap. The leading men follow the passage the engineers have marked. Riflemen lie along a field boundary as a stretcher passes behind them. The NCO stops a man taking a shortcut and points to the exposed shell.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · 26 August 1918\n\nThe cook holds a lid down as hot soup splashes over the cart. A gun wagon passes the junction towards the Scarpe. His cart jolts after it, the loose catch wrapped in sacking.\n\nOnly a patch of dry ground remains at the new position. He sets the food against a broken wall as men bring enamel mugs, still looking forward. When the bottom of the pot shows, another party arrives outside.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("一九一八年八月二十六日，斯卡尔普方向的协约国推进重返旧战线经过的白垩田野。加拿大部队越过原有阵位，德军后卫依托村落与剩余铁丝防守。炮击在接近路上翻出遗弃弹药和未爆弹。\n\n本连跟随检查受损通道的工兵。步兵在炮火支援下推进，携弹队从旧障碍缺口接近。德军枪位照看部分田界，仍在抵抗的守军与此前战斗的残骸交错分布，前进和后送伤员都受这些地段影响。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · 26 August 1918\n\nThe cook holds a lid down as hot soup splashes over the cart. A gun wagon passes the junction towards the Scarpe. His cart jolts after it, the loose catch wrapped in sacking.\n\nOnly a patch of dry ground remains at the new position. He sets the food against a broken wall as men bring enamel mugs, still looking forward. When the bottom of the pot shows, another party arrives outside.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("On 26 August 1918, the Allied advance along the Scarpe returns to chalk fields crossed by earlier fronts. Canadian troops move through old positions while German rear guards defend villages and remaining wire. Shellfire has exposed abandoned ammunition and unexploded shells along routes needed by the attackers.\n\nThe company follows engineers examining the damaged passages. Infantry advance with artillery support, and ammunition parties approach through gaps in the old obstacles. German guns cover parts of the field boundaries. The sector combines active resistance with debris left by earlier fighting, affecting both movement forward and evacuation to the rear.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Scarpe · 26 August 1918\n\nThe cook holds a lid down as hot soup splashes over the cart. A gun wagon passes the junction towards the Scarpe. His cart jolts after it, the loose catch wrapped in sacking.\n\nOnly a patch of dry ground remains at the new position. He sets the food against a broken wall as men bring enamel mugs, still looking forward. When the bottom of the pot shows, another party arrives outside.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月26日\n\n炊事兵把锅盖压住，滚汤仍从车沿溅到靴上。炮车刚过斯卡尔普方向的路口，送饭的车便跟着颠过去。他用麻布堵住松开的盖扣。\n\n新阵地只留了一小块干处，他把饭桶放到残墙下。士兵拿着搪瓷杯轮流来舀，目光还朝着前面。锅底露出来时，后一队的脚步刚在墙外响起。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。")},
