    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n工兵把绳索绑在运河岸边的断桩上，先试过纤道下的斜坡。烟幕遮住对岸，靴底碰到的石块不断往水里滑。他扶住绳结，让后一人把木料传下。\n\n湿木板横过一道裂口，水面上映出短促的枪光。工兵把最后一根绳压到坡土里，给上岸的人让开。对岸开始传回喊声，他仍低头拧紧松动的结。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe sapper ties a rope to a broken post and tests the slope beneath the canal towpath. Smoke hides the far bank. Stones under his boots keep sliding into the water.\n\nWet boards span a crack as brief muzzle flashes show in the water. He pins the last rope into the bank and lets men pass. Shouts come back from the far side; he bends to tighten another knot.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe sapper ties a rope to a broken post and tests the slope beneath the canal towpath. Smoke hides the far bank. Stones under his boots keep sliding into the water.\n\nWet boards span a crack as brief muzzle flashes show in the water. He pins the last rope into the bank and lets men pass. Shouts come back from the far side; he bends to tighten another knot.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 一九一八年十月十七日\n\n铁路切口里传出炮声，列车还在掩护后方撤运。雨水顺路堤流下，工兵贴着坡脚接近铁轨。步兵在两侧展开，反装甲枪组寻找能看见车体的位置。\n\n公路上挤着运弹车辆和担架，河谷入口越来越窄。观察员爬到高处，把列车的枪位报回。枪组搬开挡在脚边的枕木，远处的车轮仍未转动。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · Seventeen October nineteen eighteen\n\nGunfire comes from the railway cutting. The train is still covering the evacuation. Rain runs down the embankment as engineers approach the rails along its foot. Infantry spread to either side; the anti-armour crew searches for a view of the carriage.\n\nAmmunition vehicles and stretchers crowd the road into the valley. An observer climbs higher and reports the train's guns. The crew moves a sleeper out of its way. Beyond the cutting, the visible wheels have not yet begun to turn.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October nineteen eighteen.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("一九一八年十月十七日，协约国沿塞勒河进攻。德军后卫掩护部队与物资撤离，河谷里的道路、路堤和铁路切口承载交通。湿冷天气限制通行，协约国观察员寻找俯瞰守军后路的位置。\n\n本连所在的局部地段，一列武装列车仍在切口掩护撤运。工兵接近铁路，步兵沿路堤展开，反装甲武器攻击车载枪炮。附近公路也运送弹药与伤员，多路交通聚向狭窄河谷入口，阵位两侧的动静难以看清。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("The Allied attack along the Selle begins on 17 October 1918. German rear guards cover the withdrawal of troops and stores through a valley crossed by river roads, embankments and railway cuttings. Wet weather restricts traffic while Allied observers seek positions overlooking the routes behind the defence.\n\nIn the company's sector, an armed train remains in a cutting to cover evacuation. Engineers approach the railway while infantry spread along the embankment and anti-armour weapons engage the train's guns. The surrounding roads also carry ammunition and casualties, concentrating several movements around the same narrow valley approaches.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月17日\n\n铁路工把提灯放在枕木旁，用锤子敲过松动的道钉。塞勒河谷的车站还冒着烟，路堤后传来列车枪炮声。他贴着切口把损坏处画在纸上。\n\n一段钢轨被弹片削开，接头不能再靠拧紧螺栓修好。他把工具背到肩上，沿旁边的沟向前走。后面的运输队停住，提灯在没人经过的铁轨边继续亮着。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Selle Valley · 17 October 1918\n\nThe railway worker leaves his lamp by a sleeper and taps loose spikes with a hammer. Smoke hangs over the Selle station. Guns sound behind the embankment as he sketches the damaged line.\n\nA shell has cut the rail, beyond what tightening bolts can mend. He shoulders his tools and follows the ditch forward. The transport party behind him stops; the lamp keeps burning beside the unused track.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n手推车停在路边，车上的包袱用绳子扎着。加拿大部队正在接近城市，居民还没有离开全部街区。观察员伏在果园边，仔细辨认残墙之间的枪口。\n\n担架队从军车旁走过，步枪手沿浅沟靠近出口。炮兵等着前沿报回位置，军士让后队暂留墙下。街道深处开了一扇门，观察员把望远镜转了过去。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA handcart stands beside the road, its bundles tied with string. Canadian troops are approaching the town, where civilians remain in the streets. An observer lies at the orchard edge, studying a muzzle between the broken walls.\n\nA stretcher party passes the military vehicles. Riflemen follow a shallow ditch towards the exit. The batteries wait for a position from the forward posts. The NCO keeps the following men under the wall. A door opens farther down the street, and the observer turns his glasses.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月初，加拿大部队逼近瓦朗谢讷。德军外围阵位控制入城道路，城内仍住着平民。断墙、果园和浅沟限制视野，协约国炮兵观察员核对居民区附近的射界。\n\n本连在城外接近地段行动，更广地段有加拿大部队推进。军车、平民手推车和担架共用道路，德军枪位仍在出口与田界附近。战斗靠近有人居住的街道，炮火支援和后续部队通行都需要清楚辨认前方，不能仅凭远处动静判断。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("Canadian troops approach Valenciennes at the beginning of November 1918. German positions around the outskirts cover the roads into a town still inhabited by civilians. Broken walls, orchards and shallow ditches limit observation, while Allied artillery observers check the firing areas near the settlement.\n\nThe company operates on these outer approaches beside Canadian formations in the wider sector. Military vehicles, civilian carts and stretchers share the roads. German guns remain near the exits and field boundaries. The fighting takes place close to occupied streets, where artillery support and the movement of following troops depend on careful observation.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n翻译兵在瓦朗谢讷城外接住一辆手推车，车轮卡在碎砖间。老人指着街口，他听完便在地图上添一条窄线。车上的布包下露出半只裂开的盘子。\n\n炮兵联络官来问哪条街还有居民，翻译兵把铅笔移到另一块屋地。城里再次传来枪声，手推车便向沟边退了一点。他扶住车把，等道路前面让出空处。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe interpreter steadies a handcart outside Valenciennes, its wheel caught in brick rubble. An old man points down the street. A narrow line goes onto the map; a cracked plate shows beneath the bundles.\n\nThe artillery liaison officer asks which streets still have inhabitants. The pencil moves to another block of houses. Gunfire starts in town and the cart edges towards the ditch; the interpreter holds it until the road clears.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日\n\n当天的作战命令仍送到了连部，工兵带着工具走向运河。别处停战的消息已经传来，眼前的德军哨位却还在射击。城郊道路上有人推着家当经过。\n\n步枪手沿渡口接近，军士让担架队留在墙边。后续部队等着前面的回报，携弹手把箱盖重新压紧。运河对岸冒出枪口的火光，传令兵又伏了下去。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · Four November nineteen eighteen\n\nThe day's orders reach headquarters. Sappers carry their tools towards the canal. News of armistices elsewhere has arrived, but the German posts ahead are still firing. A cart of household goods passes along the road through the outskirts.\n\nRiflemen approach the crossing. The NCO keeps the stretcher party beside a wall while the following troops wait for a report. A bearer presses his ammunition lid shut. A muzzle flashes across the canal, and the runner lies down again beside the ditch.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at eleven on eleven November.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月四日，协约国向桑布尔方向进攻，新西兰部队在另一段战线接近勒凯努瓦。运河、居民区和德军后卫仍阻挡通行。其他地区停战的消息已到，西线却尚未停火。\n\n本连在运河接近路与城郊道路附近行动，工兵查看剩余障碍，步兵面对照看通路的德军哨位。居民区仍有平民，后续部队、弹药与伤员使用同样路线。渡口和当地出口周围的战斗继续，各连仍接收当天作战命令。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("On 4 November 1918, Allied forces attack towards the Sambre while New Zealand troops approach Le Quesnoy on another part of the front. Canals, settlements and German rear guards still obstruct movement. Reports of armistices elsewhere have not brought a ceasefire to the Western Front.\n\nThe company operates near canal approaches and the roads through the outskirts. Engineers examine remaining obstacles while infantry face German posts overlooking the passages. Civilians are still present in the settlements. Following troops, ammunition and casualties use the same routes as fighting continues around the crossings and local exits.")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。")},
    {TEXT("阵中日记 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n牧师把湿书放在城外的石阶上，先扶住一道快倒的门。桑布尔方向还有枪声，经过的人问有没有新的电报。他摇头，把书塞回外衣里。\n\n教堂窗玻璃落了一地，墙角的长凳还可坐人。牧师把它拖到避风处，替归来的士兵腾出一点空位。渡口的枪声稍歇，门外又有靴子踏过碎玻璃。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("WAR DIARY · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe chaplain lays his wet book on a stone step and steadies a falling door. Guns still sound towards the Sambre. Men passing ask whether another dispatch has come.\n\nGlass covers the church floor, though a bench remains in the corner. He drags it out of the wind for soldiers returning from the line. The firing at the crossing eases; more boots pass through the glass outside.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 一九一七年四月九日\n\n前哨的电话只有杂音。雨雪遮住白垩坡，英军已越过被炮击打断的前沿。洞穴里的士兵重新携枪出壕，枪位向连部报来缺弹。\n\n反击队在白垩路旁集合。联络兵循断线找去，坡后的机枪继续射击。携弹手把箱子搬过担架，几个失联哨位尚未报回点名结果。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · Nine April nineteen seventeen\n\nThe outpost telephone gives only static. Sleet hides the chalk slope and British troops have crossed the damaged forward line. Men come out of the caves with their rifles. The gun posts report that ammunition is running short.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble beside the chalk road. A runner follows the broken wire while the guns beyond the crest keep firing. Bearers carry their boxes past stretchers. Several silent posts have yet to return their rolls.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("一九一七年四月九日，英军在阿拉斯的进攻打乱了德军前沿。雨雪和炮火遮住白垩坡面，洞穴与壕沟仍联系着部分阵位，前哨电话却只剩杂音，数处枪位已与后方失联。\n\n本连沿白垩路集结，准备实施局部反击。这一地段包括山脊接近线，以及向幸存哨位输送弹药的通路。英军越过受损的前沿壕沟，坡后的德军枪组继续射击。前线各支点情况不一，人员和补给仍须通过高地两侧。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("The British attack at Arras on 9 April 1917 has disrupted the German forward line. Rain, snow and bombardment obscure the chalk slopes. Some posts remain connected through caves and trenches, but the outpost telephone gives only interference, and several gun positions have lost contact with the rear.\n\nThe company is assembling a local counterattack along the chalk road. Its sector includes the ridge approaches and the routes supplying the surviving posts. British troops are advancing beyond the damaged front trenches, while German crews behind the high ground try to maintain fire and restore contact.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 阿拉斯以东 · 1917年4月9日\n\n线路兵沿白垩沟找到一截断线，铜丝上粘着湿粉。前哨的电话已经失声，雨雪里只能辨认最近的枪位。他用牙咬住套管，把两头绞在一起。\n\n试话时，另一端先传来炮声，再传来半句坐标。线路兵在壕壁上记下地址，往松土里压好接头。反击队从身旁穿过，他把线圈举高，让最后一人先走。\n\n阿拉斯攻势与法军埃纳河攻势同属春季作战计划。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Arras · 9 April 1917\n\nThe linesman finds a broken wire in the chalk ditch, its copper coated with wet dust. The outpost telephone is silent. Sleet leaves only the nearest gun post visible.\n\nWhen he tests the joint, gunfire comes through before half a coordinate. He marks the address on the trench wall and buries the splice in loose soil. A counterattack party passes; he lifts his coil clear of the last man.\n\nArras and the French attack on the Aisne formed parts of the spring offensive plan.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 一九一七年四月中旬\n\n地下掩体的出口落满碎砖，换防人员弯腰钻出。化工厂外已有英军接近，枪手隔着断墙观察壕口。电话线穿过厂房废墟，接线兵只找到一截断头。\n\n反击队沿铁路堤下集合，携弹兵把箱子交给仍在射击的枪组。军士指着被炮火切断的交通壕，重新安排去路。厂墙另一面的脚步听得很近。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April nineteen seventeen\n\nBricks cover the dugout exit. Reliefs bend low to come out. British troops are approaching the chemical works, and a gunner watches the trench mouth through a broken wall. The linesman finds only a severed end among the factory ruins.\n\nCounterattack parties assemble below the railway bank. Bearers hand boxes to a gun still firing. The NCO points to the communication trench cut by shellfire and directs men along another passage. Footsteps sound close on the other side of the wall.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until sixteen May.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("一九一七年四月中旬，勒厄化工厂仍是阿拉斯以东道路上的德军支点。英军正在进入外围接近地段。厂墙、铁路工事和地下掩体构成相连阵位，炮火却已损坏其间通道。\n\n本连准备向受威胁的外围壕沟反击。枪组隔着破墙照看缺口，携弹兵使用尚存掩蔽路线。接近壕关系着厂区交通，一旦中断，部分阵位就难以接到换防人员和弹药。铁路堤与残墙分割视野，守军无法从一处看清整片外围。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("The chemical works at Roeux remain a German strongpoint on the roads east of Arras. In mid-April 1917, British troops are pressing into the outer approaches. Factory walls, railway earthworks and underground shelters give the defenders connected positions, although shellfire has damaged the passages between them.\n\nThe company's counterattack is directed towards the threatened outer trenches. Gun crews cover gaps through the broken masonry, and ammunition bearers use the remaining sheltered routes. Loss of an approach trench would interrupt traffic to the works, leaving some factory positions separated from their reliefs and supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 勒厄 · 1917年4月中旬\n\n修理兵把油灯拆开放在厂房楼梯上，灯芯里积满砖粉。地下掩体又涌出一队人，皮带擦得墙灰往下掉。他把灯罩藏到膝间，等他们走完。\n\n墙外的枪声很近，地下却只看得到火苗照出的台阶。修理兵捻去灯芯上的黑结，把灯挂回出口。又有人把一只破灯递来，玻璃里夹着细小弹屑。\n\n阿拉斯攻势延续至五月十六日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Roeux · Mid-April 1917\n\nThe lamp repairer opens an oil lamp on the factory stairs. Brick dust has clogged its wick. Men climb from the shelter, their belts scraping plaster from the wall.\n\nFiring is close outside, but below ground the flame lights only a few steps. He clears the blackened wick and hangs the lamp by the exit. Another broken lamp is handed down, with tiny fragments caught in its glass.\n\nThe Arras offensive continued until 16 May.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 一九一七年五月三日\n\n掩蔽部里响起上壕的口令，枪榴弹正在胸墙外爆炸。铁丝之间还压着四月留下的残骸，英澳步兵又从缺口接近。枪组把弹带拖到射位旁边。\n\n携弹兵贴着深壕前送，换防队在转角停步。相邻哨位只见烟尘，军士让一名联络兵过去查看。坡面上露出钢盔又消失，枪手转动枪架追着看。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · Three May nineteen seventeen\n\nThe order to man the trench reaches the dugout as rifle grenades burst outside the parapet. April's wreckage still weighs down the wire. British and Australian infantry approach its gaps again. The crew pulls a belt beside the mounting.\n\nBearers follow the deep trench while reliefs halt at a traverse. Smoke hides the neighbouring post. The NCO sends a runner to find it. A helmet appears above the slope and disappears; the gunner turns his mounting to search the ground again.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("一九一七年五月三日，澳大利亚与英国部队在布勒库尔重新进攻。德军仍守着兴登堡线铁丝后的纵深壕，四月战斗留下的残骸尚未清走。后方通道把弹药和换防人员送往幸存哨位。\n\n本连位于这套壕沟的一段，分散枪组照看铁丝受损地段，枪榴弹正落向壕角和胸墙。英澳步兵沿缺口接近。地下掩体支撑着防御，但外围壕沟遭到攻击，相邻哨位的联系也受威胁。断墙与弹坑使接近者时隐时现。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("Australian and British attacks resume at Bullecourt on 3 May 1917. German defenders still hold deep trenches behind the Hindenburg wire, where the wreckage of the April battle remains. Rear passages carry ammunition and reliefs towards posts that survived the earlier fighting.\n\nThe company occupies part of this trench system. Its dispersed guns cover damaged sections of wire, while rifle grenades are falling around the corners and parapets. British and Australian infantry are approaching the gaps. The shelter network supports the defence, but bombardment and attacks on the outer trenches threaten contact between adjacent posts.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布勒库尔 · 1917年5月3日\n\n送水兵把水桶放到壕角，桶箍撞在枪架上响了一声。掩蔽部里的人正往上走，白垩粉落进还没盖好的桶口。他用外衣遮住水面。\n\n机枪旁的一只水壶已经空了，他侧身挤过去填满。胸墙外的枪榴弹又炸开，桶盖在脚边滚了一圈。前队喊着要水，他把壶递出去，桶里只剩浅浅一层。\n\n澳大利亚与英国部队于五月再攻布勒库尔。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bullecourt · 3 May 1917\n\nThe water carrier sets a bucket at the traverse, its hoop striking a gun mount. Men climb from the dugout. Chalk falls through the uncovered top, and he shelters the water with his coat.\n\nAn empty vessel waits beside the machine gun; he squeezes through to refill it. A rifle grenade bursts beyond the parapet and the bucket lid rolls away. Water is called for ahead; little remains at the bottom.\n\nAustralian and British troops attacked Bullecourt again in May.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 一九一七年六月七日\n\n旧壕入口被土埋住，报告里标出的树也找不到了。地下爆炸过后，英军炮火越过山脊。幸存枪位隔着新坑射击，联络兵爬上坑岸再伏下来。\n\n前来的步枪手沿碎土收拢人员，携弹兵试着下到塌壕里。对面出现新的英军枪口，军士把地图折回原处。他要找的交通壕已在陡壁另一面。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · Seven June nineteen seventeen\n\nEarth has buried the old trench entrance. The tree marked in the report has disappeared. British shellfire passes over the ridge after the underground explosions. A surviving gun fires across a fresh crater; the runner climbs its lip and drops down.\n\nArriving riflemen gather scattered men along the broken slope. Bearers try to reach the collapsed trench. A new British muzzle appears opposite. The NCO folds his map again. The communication trench he needs lies beyond the steep new bank.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("一九一七年六月七日破晓前，梅西讷的地下爆炸埋住部分德军前线。英军炮火与步兵随后越过山脊。旧壕入口没入碎土，新坑壁截断通往幸存枪位的道路，邻近阵位陆续失去联系。\n\n本连向受创地段移动，收拢守军，恢复联络。部分枪组仍从弹坑另一面射击，报告中的旧地标却已改变。人员和弹药越过破碎坡面赶来，英军在初次进攻所得地段修筑阵位，新的枪口开始照看坑岸。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("The mine explosions at Messines before dawn on 7 June 1917 have buried parts of the German front. British artillery and infantry follow across the ridge. Old trench entrances are lost beneath rubble, and fresh crater walls interrupt the routes to surviving gun positions.\n\nThe company is moving towards the shattered sector to gather defenders and restore contact. Some crews are still firing from positions beyond the craters, but reports no longer match the former landmarks. Men and ammunition approach through damaged slopes while British formations establish themselves on ground taken in the opening attack.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷山脊 · 1917年6月7日\n\n工兵用锹柄探到旧掩体入口，松土又从顶上落下。爆破后的坑岸遮住了原来的树，地下木撑只露出一角。他跪下把土拨开，里面传来敲击声。\n\n他把一根横木压在裂口下，叫身旁的人递来铁锹。地面上的枪位已经换到坑边，电话线也垂进新沟里。木撑挪动了一点，他停住手，听里面的人再敲一次。\n\n梅西讷进攻以地下爆破摧毁山脊上的德军阵位。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Messines Ridge · 7 June 1917\n\nThe sapper probes a buried shelter entrance with his spade handle. More loose soil falls from above. A corner of timber shows beneath the crater edge; tapping comes from inside.\n\nHe braces a beam under the crack and calls for another spade. Guns above have moved to the crater rim, and telephone wire hangs into the new ditch. The support shifts slightly; he stops and listens for another tap.\n\nUnderground mines destroyed German ridge positions as the Messines attack opened.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 一九一七年六月九日\n\n集合处的军士指着坑岸，新接近路从那里转过去。山脊上的英军正在加固胸墙，旧德军壕道已被爆破切断。步枪手轮流爬高，辨认幸存哨位的方向。\n\n携弹队从东坡赶来，鞋上带着松土。枪组在狭路尽头等候，前面的联络兵尚未回来。反击队沿坡伏下，能看见对面有人搬动新装满的土袋。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · Nine June nineteen seventeen\n\nThe NCO points from the assembly place towards a crater lip. The new approach turns there. British troops strengthen the ridge parapet above German trenches cut by explosions. Riflemen climb in turn to locate the surviving posts.\n\nBearers arrive up the eastern slope with loose earth on their boots. The gun crew waits at the end of the narrow path. Its runner has not returned. The counterattack party lies along the bank, watching men move freshly filled sandbags on the opposite side.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("一九一七年六月九日，德军准备向梅西讷山脊实施局部反击。英军正在加固爆破后夺取的阵位，预备队聚在坡脊另一面。新弹坑和塌壕改变了原先的德军接近路。\n\n本连在山脊东面集结，向坑岸移动。幸存德军哨位需要接回后方，也需要对付新出现的英军防线。携弹队从破碎坡面间剩余通路赶来。此时英军胸墙和补给路线尚未完全整理，双方都在利用还能通行的地段组织部队。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("On 9 June 1917, German troops prepare a local counterattack towards Messines ridge. British forces are strengthening the positions taken after the mines, while their reserves gather beyond the crest. Fresh craters and collapsed trenches have altered the former German approaches.\n\nThe company assembles east of the ridge and moves towards the crater banks. Surviving German posts need contact with the rear as well as support against the new British line. Ammunition parties use the remaining passages through the broken slopes. The counterattack takes place before the new breastworks and supply routes have fully settled.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅西讷东坡 · 1917年6月9日\n\n枪组的弹带修理手把湿带铺在膝上，挤出裂开的扣眼里那一粒泥。东坡的反击队还没有出发，机枪停在狭路尽头。他把缝线从弹药盒下抽出来。\n\n坑岸上已经看得见英军搬动土袋，邻哨却迟迟没有回话。修理手逐节检查弹带，把歪掉的一发取下。命令从坡后送来，他卷好湿带，交给等在枪架旁的人。\n\n梅西讷山脊在六月的进攻中落入英军之手。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Messines · 9 June 1917\n\nThe belt repairer spreads a wet belt across his knees and picks mud from a torn pocket. The counterattack party waits on the eastern slope. Its gun stands at the end of a narrow track.\n\nBritish men move sandbags on the crater rim, but the neighbouring post gives no answer. He checks each pocket and removes a crooked round. An order arrives from behind the slope; the wet belt is rolled for the waiting gun.\n\nBritish forces captured Messines Ridge in the June attack.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 一九一七年七月三十一日\n\n携弹兵停在陷下去的木板前，箱子只能从手上传过去。前沿各枪位被水隔开，英军在雨烟中接近。壕炮组等着炮弹，守望的人不断擦去镜片上的水。\n\n一条硬路从坑岸后通过，换防队蹲在路边等候。军士让送信的人先走，又向远处枪声张望。邻近的机枪还在响，后方却没有找到过去的路。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · Thirty-one July nineteen seventeen\n\nA bearer stops at a sunken plank. His box must pass from hand to hand. Water separates the forward guns as British troops approach through rain and smoke. The mortar crew waits for ammunition. Its lookout keeps wiping the glass.\n\nA firm track passes behind the crater bank. Reliefs crouch beside it while the NCO sends a messenger ahead. He turns towards the distant firing again. The next machine gun can still be heard, but the men behind have found no path to it.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on thirty-one July.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("一九一七年七月三十一日，英军向皮尔克姆进攻。雨水和炮击使伊普尔周围田野积水，德军前沿被分成相隔的哨位。剩余硬路运送弹药、消息和换防人员，许多阵位无法直接互相观察。\n\n本连守着这片湿地的一段，枪组占据可用坑岸与掩体，壕炮弹沿尚存通路送上来。英军动静在雨烟中断续出现。道路损坏时，即使相邻枪位仍在，补给也可能中断。后方携弹队正寻找能够继续靠近前沿的地段。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("The British attack towards Pilckem begins on 31 July 1917. Rain and artillery damage have flooded the fields around Ypres, breaking the German forward area into separated posts. The remaining firm paths carry ammunition, messages and reliefs between positions that often cannot see one another.\n\nThe company defends part of this wet ground. Gun crews occupy usable banks and shelters, while mortar ammunition is carried forward along the surviving routes. British movement is visible only intermittently through rain and smoke. Damage to a path can interrupt supply even where the neighbouring gun positions remain intact.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 皮尔克姆 · 1917年7月31日\n\n修鞋兵把拔下的靴子倒过来，泥水从破缝里流出来。他用锥子穿过泡软的皮面，针线几次滑脱。木板路上的脚步停在积水前，又往旁边挪去。\n\n靴底还没缝完，主人已经伸手来取。修鞋兵递过一条布，让他先裹住裂口。壕炮弹从身旁传过去，留下的鞋印很快灌满水，针还夹在两指之间。\n\n第三次伊普尔战役于七月三十一日开始。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Pilckem · 31 July 1917\n\nThe boot repairer turns a boot upside down and pours mud from its split seam. His awl goes through the soaked leather. Footsteps stop at a flooded duckboard, then shift aside.\n\nBefore the sole is sewn, its owner reaches for it. The repairer gives him cloth to wrap the split. Mortar bombs pass along the trench; the prints they leave fill with water while the needle stays between his fingers.\n\nThe Third Battle of Ypres began on 31 July.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 一九一七年八月\n\n混凝土顶上落下灰尘，枪手把眼睛贴回射孔。农场外的田野已经积水，英军沿干路接近。送弹路经过掩体旁，换防人员侧身从弹箱之间穿过。\n\n迫击炮弹落在残墙后面，联络兵听不清邻哨的回答。军士让枪组继续守着入口，自己沿墙走到拐角。水面晃着几个倒影，干路上的脚步却停了。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August nineteen seventeen\n\nDust falls from the concrete roof. The gunner returns his eye to the loophole. Water covers the field outside the farm, and British troops follow the dry approaches. Reliefs squeeze past ammunition boxes on the track beside the shelter.\n\nMortar bombs fall behind the ruined wall. A runner cannot hear the next post's reply. The NCO leaves the crew watching the entrance and follows the wall to its corner. Reflections move on the water, but footsteps on the dry track have stopped.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("一九一七年八月，朗厄马尔克的德军依靠混凝土掩体守住积水田野。农场建筑已成废墟，部分有遮蔽的枪位仍由干路联系。伊普尔周边战斗继续，英军正从据点之间接近。\n\n本连位于这条分散防线的一段，中央送弹路供给邻近枪组和换防队，机枪照看农场周围入口。积水隔开原先较易联系的阵位，英军迫击炮和接近干路的进攻威胁补给运输。前沿各处仍能抵抗，却不能在一处看清全部接近地段。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("At Langemarck in August 1917, concrete shelters support the German defence across waterlogged fields. Farm buildings have been reduced to ruins, but some protected gun positions remain connected by dry tracks. British troops are approaching between the strongpoints as the fighting around Ypres continues.\n\nThe company occupies part of this dispersed line. The central ammunition route serves neighbouring crews and relief parties, while guns cover the approaches around ruined farms. Flooding has separated positions that once had easier contact. British mortar fire and attacks near the tracks threaten the movement needed to keep those posts supplied.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 朗厄马尔克 · 1917年8月\n\n观察员把潜望镜推过混凝土顶，镜面被雨打成一片灰。田野里的英军正沿窄路接近，他擦去水珠，再看那道农场矮墙。射孔旁的枪手等着他开口。\n\n炮弹落在墙后，镜里只剩翻动的水和泥。观察员把镜杆降回胸前，从入口换到另一面。有人经过时碰响弹箱，他扶住箱盖，示意枪手仍看着原来的路。\n\n伊普尔攻势直到秋季仍未取得预期突破。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Langemarck · August 1917\n\nThe observer raises a periscope above the concrete roof. Rain greys the glass. British troops approach along the narrow farm track, while the gunner waits beside the loophole.\n\nA shell falls behind the wall, leaving water and mud turning in the mirror. He lowers the instrument and moves to the other side of the entrance. A passing man rattles an ammunition box; he steadies its lid and points back towards the track.\n\nThe Ypres offensive failed to achieve its intended breakthrough.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 一九一七年九月\n\n观察员摊开图纸，把前沿标记向林后移了一点。英军炮火还在延伸，新胸墙已出现在树桩之间。预备队沿破路进入林地，枪组停下来等候侧翼消息。\n\n幸存哨位夹在两军之间，携弹兵不知道该在哪个壕口转弯。军士向断树后打出手势，前队逐人穿过开阔处。观察员的铅笔仍压在那条刚画出的线上。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September nineteen seventeen\n\nThe observer opens his sketch and shifts a forward mark farther into the wood. British shellfire continues to lift. New parapets appear among the stumps. Reserves enter along a broken path; the gun crew stops for news from the flank.\n\nSurviving posts lie between the forces. A bearer is unsure which trench mouth to take. The NCO signals beyond a shattered tree, and the leading men cross the open patch one at a time. The observer's pencil rests on his fresh line.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("一九一七年九月，英军在梅宁路以强大炮火支援有限推进。德军预备队在破碎林地后方集结反击，报告称英军正在林缘加固新阵位。尚存小路和坡脊限制着接近方向。\n\n本连从后方进入受威胁地段。炮兵观察员核对变化中的战线，枪组照看穿林路线。幸存德军哨位仍隔在英军推进部队与预备队之间。交通壕和小路受损，增援与弹药难以及时抵达，林间残树又遮住了部分相邻阵位。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("The British advance at the Menin Road in September 1917 is taking limited ground under heavy artillery cover. German reserves are assembling beyond the shattered woodland for a counterattack. Reports describe British troops strengthening new positions near the tree line, where surviving paths and ridges restrict the approaches.\n\nThe company moves from the rear towards this threatened sector. Artillery observers are checking the changing line, and gun crews cover routes through the woods. Surviving German posts remain between the British advance and the reserves. Broken communications and damaged tracks complicate the arrival of reinforcements and ammunition.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 梅宁路 · 1917年9月\n\n绘图员把图钉压在箱盖上，纸角仍被风掀起。林后送来的报告说旧枪位已失，他沿树桩的位置画下新线。墨瓶倾了一下，在边缘留下黑圈。\n\n预备队穿过路口，他先把各队去路画在草图上。另一个哨位没有回报，那个方框便留着空白。送图的人蹲在墙边等，他擦干纸面，把还未干的线折到里面。\n\n梅宁路进攻采用炮火支援下的有限推进。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Menin Road · September 1917\n\nThe draughtsman pins a sheet to a box lid, though wind keeps lifting its corner. A report says the old gun post is lost. He draws a new line along the stumps.\n\nReserves pass the junction as he marks their routes on a sketch. Another post has sent no report, leaving its square blank. The runner waits against the wall; the damp sheet is folded with its fresh ink inside.\n\nThe Menin Road attack used limited advances supported by artillery.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 一九一七年十一月三十日\n\n反击命令送到枪位。田野里散着上次进攻留下的战车，英军正在修补新胸墙。炮兵向接近线开火，步枪手等待 MG 08/15 枪组收好弹带。\n\n交通壕转过一处路口，前面的射孔便看不见了。携弹队在壕角让出通路，担架沿原路回送。修理场里的缴获车辆还未归队，枪手先用两肩把机枪送上坡。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · Thirty November nineteen seventeen\n\nThe counterattack order reaches the gun post. Tanks from the earlier fighting lie in the fields. British troops are repairing their new parapets. Our batteries fire on the approaches while the riflemen wait for the MG 08/15 crews to pack their belts.\n\nA bend in the communication trench hides the next loophole. Bearers stand aside at the junction and stretchers pass back along the route. Captured vehicles have not left the repair yard; the crew carries its gun up the slope on their shoulders.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("一九一七年十一月三十日，德军开始反击康布雷突出部。此前的英军坦克攻势打乱了兴登堡线附近的道路与阵位，英军正在加固所得地段。损坏和缴获坦克仍留在德军后方。\n\n本连的步枪手与MG 08/15枪组向受威胁交通线前进，德军炮兵迎击接近路上的英军装甲。深壕切过开阔田野，遮住阵位之间的移动。双方仍依靠这些公路和路口输送补给，旧有前线已经改变，部分壕道方向尚未调整。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("On 30 November 1917, German forces begin their counterattack around the Cambrai salient. The earlier British tank offensive has disrupted roads and positions near the Hindenburg Line. British troops are strengthening captured ground, while damaged and captured tanks remain behind the German front.\n\nThe company advances towards the threatened communications with riflemen and MG 08/15 crews. German artillery engages British armour along the approaches. Deep trenches interrupt the open fields and conceal movement between positions. The counterattack is directed through this altered front, where supply roads and junctions remain important to both armies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷突出部 · 1917年11月30日\n\n修理工把扳手放在缴获战车的履带上，手背仍沾着旧油。前沿要车的消息已经送到，车里拆开的零件还铺在地板上。他俯身试了试卡住的连杆。\n\n修理场外的炮火开始了，运输车卷起干土从门口经过。修理工把一枚螺母放回铁盒，叫助手拿来另一根销。发动机暂时没有响，前线的电话又催来一次。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Salient · 30 November 1917\n\nThe mechanic rests his spanner on a captured tank's track, oil still on his hands. The front has asked for vehicles. Dismantled parts cover the floor while he tests a jammed linkage.\n\nThe guns start outside the workshop and transport passes the entrance in dry dust. He returns a nut to its tin and asks for another pin. The engine is still silent when the front telephones again.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the ground gained by the British at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 一九一七年十一月三十日\n\n浅洼里的人压低枪口，前面林缘又响起一阵机枪声。英军把枪位转向道路，突出部的伤员还在往外送。反击队沿受损壕沟接近，携弹兵跟着最后一人。\n\n断树把邻队遮住，炮兵联络兵在壕口停下来核对位置。道路上有车辆逆着退回的人流前行。军士伏到沟边，伸手拦住准备穿过缺口的步枪手。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · Thirty November nineteen seventeen\n\nMen in the hollow lower their muzzles as another burst comes from the tree line. British guns face the road, where wounded men are still leaving the salient. The counterattack follows a damaged trench with bearers behind the last rifleman.\n\nBroken trees hide the next party. An artillery runner stops at the trench mouth to check his position. Vehicles move against the returning traffic on the road. The NCO lies beside the ditch and stops a rifleman about to cross the gap.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("德军在康布雷附近的反击正在接近布尔隆林。英军守着突出部出口，同时把伤员与部分部队送往后方。弹药车辆仍逆向前行，新的英军枪位照看破碎林地旁的道路。双方都在争夺出口交通。\n\n本连沿浅洼和受损壕沟接近，炮兵联络随着战线变化重新建立。步枪手在林缘遭遇连续阵位，英军防御后面的道路仍在使用。断树遮住交通，也遮住邻近德军队伍；携弹兵正沿尚存路线跟上前沿。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("The German counterattack near Cambrai is reaching the approaches to Bourlon Wood. British forces are defending the salient's exits while moving wounded men and some troops towards the rear. Ammunition traffic continues in the opposite direction. New British gun positions cover the roads beside the broken woodland.\n\nThe company approaches these exits through hollows and damaged trenches. Artillery liaison is being restored as the front changes, while riflemen encounter successive positions near the tree line. The roads remain in use behind the British defence. Broken trees restrict observation of both the traffic and neighbouring German parties.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 布尔隆林 · 1917年11月30日\n\n护送兵在布尔隆林外扶住一个走不稳的人，先把他的步枪挎到肩上。林缘的机枪开始射击，浅洼里的人都低下头。伤员手里还攥着剪开的袖扣。\n\n路口有车逆着人流往前走，护送兵让到断树后等候。炮兵联络兵经过，问他们从哪个壕口出来。他指向林里，又把伤员扶起，沿有脚印的那一侧继续走。\n\n德军反击收复了英军在康布雷取得的部分土地。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Bourlon Wood · 30 November 1917\n\nThe escort supports an unsteady man outside Bourlon Wood and takes his rifle. A gun starts at the tree line. Heads go down in the hollow; the casualty still holds a cut sleeve button.\n\nA vehicle moves against the foot traffic, forcing them behind a broken tree. An artillery runner asks which trench they came from. The escort points into the wood, helps the man stand and follows the side of the road marked by footprints.\n\nThe German counterattack recovered part of the British gains at Cambrai.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 一九一八年二月\n\n壕边的雪里有新脚印，前哨却没有回话。接线兵收起断头，顺着湿沟查找另一段线。轻装队把松动的器材系紧，等天色暗下来再离开胸墙。\n\n留守的枪组听见远处零星射击，换防队已经到达后壕。巡逻队在拐角留下一个人，前队消失在铁丝后面。军士靠着壕壁等候，手里的电话没有响。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February nineteen eighteen\n\nFresh tracks mark the snow beside the trench, but the outpost gives no answer. The linesman collects a broken end and searches along the wet ditch. A light party fastens its loose equipment before leaving the parapet after dark.\n\nThe remaining gun crew hears scattered shots. Reliefs have reached the rear trench. The patrol leaves a man at the bend and vanishes beyond the wire. The duty NCO waits against the wall, with the silent telephone receiver still held beside his ear.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("一九一八年二月，康布雷附近的德军继续修筑壕沟，在冬季前线组织巡逻。铁丝前出现新脚印，一处前哨没有回话。雨雪遮住低田，双方换防活动也使前方动静难以辨认。\n\n本连集结轻装队，准备天黑后查看前沿。相邻壕道与湿沟提供短距离接近路，视野十分有限。巡逻队身后仍有哨兵值守，电话联络也在尝试恢复。这次行动针对本地前哨的异常，附近阵线尚未发生大规模变化。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("By February 1918, German troops near Cambrai are repairing trenches and conducting patrols along the winter front. Fresh tracks have appeared before the wire, and an outpost has not answered. Rain and snow obscure the low fields, while relief movements on both sides make activity difficult to identify.\n\nThe company assembles a light party to investigate the forward ground after dark. Nearby trenches and wet ditches provide short approaches with little visibility. Sentries remain behind the patrol, and attempts to restore the outpost telephone continue. The action concerns this local interruption along an otherwise established sector.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 康布雷前线 · 1918年2月\n\n勤务兵把怀表放在掩体桌上，拨针的人刚报完出发时刻。他听见外面的巡逻扣紧装具，又用干布擦去表盖上的霜。炉里的余火只照亮半张地图。\n\n军官带走地图，桌上只剩一枚脱下的手套。勤务兵把表交回去，到入口看看巡逻是否已经出壕。照明弹升起时，门帘被风掀开，他伸手把它压住。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Cambrai Front · February 1918\n\nThe orderly lays a pocket watch on the dugout table after the departure time is read. Outside, a patrol tightens its equipment. He wipes frost from the case in the low stove light.\n\nThe officer takes the map, leaving a glove behind. The orderly returns the watch and checks whether the patrol has left. A flare rises; wind lifts the entrance curtain, and he holds it down with his hand.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 一九一八年三月二十一日\n\n先遣步枪手越过破壕，雾里只看得见最近的人。英军第五集团军的支点之间有缺口，炮火继续向后延伸。枪组抬着器材跟上，携弹队还在寻找穿过旧铁丝的路。\n\n前队已经接近公路，侧翼却没有报回位置。联络兵在壕口摊开地图，军士向他指了指身后的长路。弹箱上的绳子磨松了，携弹手停下重新打结。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · Twenty-one March nineteen eighteen\n\nThe leading riflemen cross a broken trench. Only the nearest men show in the fog. Gaps open between British Fifth Army strongpoints while the barrage moves farther back. The gun crew follows with its equipment; bearers search for a path through the old wire.\n\nThe road is close ahead, but the flank has sent no position. A runner opens his map at the trench mouth. The NCO points back along their lengthening route. A loose rope on an ammunition box needs tying again.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on twenty-one March.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("一九一八年三月二十一日，米夏埃尔攻势以炮击英军前线和后方联络开始。浓雾限制观察，德军突击队寻找支点之间的缺口。英军第五集团军正面宽阔，阵位分散，幸存哨位仍在接近路上抵抗。\n\n本连穿过受损壕沟，向旧前线之外的道路推进。机枪组与携弹队跟随先遣步枪手，炮火逐渐移向纵深，侧翼报告却还不完整。进入英军阵位的部队与原先补给路线之间，距离正在拉长。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("Operation Michael begins on 21 March 1918 with artillery striking the British front and rear communications. Fog restricts observation as German assault parties seek gaps between strongpoints. The British Fifth Army's wide sector offers separated positions, but surviving posts continue to resist along the approaches.\n\nThe company advances through damaged trenches towards roads beyond the former front. Machine gun crews and ammunition parties follow the leading riflemen. The artillery is shifting deeper while flank reports remain incomplete. Forward movement has extended the distance from the German supply routes to the troops entering British positions.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 圣康坦方向 · 1918年3月21日\n\n工兵把剪钳推到旧铁丝下面，雾里只看得清最近的一根立柱。先遣队已向破壕走去，他压住钳柄，让断股贴着地面落下。棉手套上挂满细刺。\n\n枪架从缺口抬过去，后面的人又把弹箱卡在丝上。工兵转回半步，剪开剩下那一股。炮声向更远处延伸，他把断丝卷到立柱旁，跟着最后一只箱子离开。\n\n三月二十一日，德军发动米夏埃尔攻势。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March."), TEXT("WAR LOG · St Quentin Sector · 21 March 1918\n\nThe sapper slips his cutters beneath old wire. Only the nearest post shows in the fog. The leading troops reach the broken trench as he lowers a severed strand to the ground.\n\nA gun mount passes the gap, but an ammunition box catches behind it. He cuts the remaining strand. The guns shift farther away; he rolls the loose wire against the post and leaves after the last box.\n\nGermany launched Operation Michael on 21 March.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 一九一八年四月九日\n\n枪架在软土里陷下去，后面的携弹兵赶来帮忙。前队已经越过河沟，向葡英阵位之间的缺口前进。路口还有英军哨位射击，水沟两侧的人都伏下来。\n\n军士沿较硬的地面寻找邻队，传令兵从另一条沟里回来。后方的补给尚在渡口，枪组只能先把现有弹箱搬上岸。前队的手势隔着水面显得很小。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · Nine April nineteen eighteen\n\nThe mounting sinks into soft ground. Bearers behind the crew help lift it. The leading men have crossed the ditch towards a gap between Portuguese and British positions. A British post still fires from the junction, forcing both banks down.\n\nThe NCO follows firmer ground in search of the next party. A runner returns through another ditch. Supplies remain at the crossing. The crew carries its remaining boxes onto the bank, watching a small hand signal from the men across the water.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("一九一八年四月九日，德军乔治特攻势越过利斯河低地，攻击葡萄牙与英军阵位。水沟和河道截断平田，前排继续推进，后面的携弹队却仍依靠同样有限的道路与河岸入口。\n\n本连向联系当地通路的路口前进。机枪组沿较实地面移动，突击分队穿过相邻河沟，英军哨位仍分散在这一地段。积水、损坏通信和补给距离使德军先遣部队难以互相联系，后续人员正在从原有接近路赶来。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("On 9 April 1918, German forces open Georgette across the Lys lowlands against Portuguese and British positions. Ditches and watercourses interrupt the flat fields. The initial pressure is carrying the attack forward, while ammunition parties behind the infantry must use the same restricted roads and riverbank approaches.\n\nThe company advances towards a junction linking the local routes. Machine gun crews move along the firmer ground as assault parties pass through neighbouring ditches. British posts remain separated across the sector. Water, damaged communications and the distance from the following supplies complicate contact between German forward groups.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 利斯河低地 · 1918年4月9日\n\n信鸽兵把鸽笼靠在利斯河沟旁，鸟爪扣着被雨打湿的木条。刚递来的纸片只有一行地址，他把它卷进小管。河对岸的枪声让笼里的翅膀碰响两次。\n\n前队已经越过河沟，渡口的车辆还没有动。他掀开笼门，把鸟托到避风的一面。鸽子飞过低墙便看不见了，空笼里只留下沾在门轴上的一片灰羽。\n\n德军四月攻势把战斗扩展到利斯河地区。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Lys Lowlands · 9 April 1918\n\nThe pigeon keeper sets a basket beside a Lys ditch. Claws grip its wet wooden slats. He rolls a message bearing a single address into the capsule as gunfire disturbs the wings inside.\n\nThe leading troops have crossed the ditch, but vehicles wait at the ford. He opens the basket and lifts the bird out of the wind. It disappears beyond a low wall; a grey feather remains at the hinge.\n\nGermany extended its spring offensive to the Lys in April.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 一九一八年四月二十四日\n\n村口的战车转向路口，步兵借着车侧经过果园。英军装甲在近郊开火，断墙后也有步枪声。车组看不见小巷，前队停在墙角，等后面的人靠近。\n\n携弹兵沿村道赶来，军士让一班步枪手进入侧巷。履带声绕过建筑又传回来，车影已经被挡住。门洞里一阵射击，走在最前面的人立刻贴住砖墙。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · Twenty-four April nineteen eighteen\n\nA tank turns at the village entrance and infantry pass the orchard beside its flank. British armour fires from the outskirts. Rifles answer behind a broken wall. The crew cannot see the lane, where the leading men wait for those behind.\n\nBearers arrive along the village road. The NCO sends a section into a side alley. Tracks can be heard beyond the buildings, but the vehicle is hidden. A burst comes from a doorway and the first rifleman presses against the bricks.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("一九一八年四月二十四日，德军进攻来到维莱布勒托讷，这里控制着通往亚眠铁路中心的道路。步兵和坦克进入村庄，英军装甲从近郊开火。破损建筑与果园边界把战斗分成短促、半隐蔽的接近地段。\n\n本连在德军车辆周围行动，随着它们向村口移动。墙巷之间仍有英军步兵，部分位置不在车组视野内。村道输送后续人员和弹药，建筑与交叉路遮住移动，装甲与步兵时常失去直接观察。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("The German attack on 24 April 1918 reaches Villers-Bretonneux, which guards roads towards the Amiens railway centre. Infantry and tanks enter the village while British armour fires from the nearby outskirts. Broken buildings and orchard boundaries divide the fighting into short, partly concealed approaches.\n\nThe company operates around the German vehicles as they move towards the village exits. British infantry remain among the walls and lanes, beyond parts of the tank crews' view. Roads through the settlement carry following troops and ammunition. Contact between armour and infantry is interrupted when movement passes behind buildings or across junctions.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 维莱布勒托讷 · 1918年4月24日\n\n车组助手从发动机旁钻出来，袖口在热管上擦过。村口的战车正在转向，他摸到松开的扣带，把器材重新系紧。果园外有人敲响车壁。\n\n前面的车组看不见侧巷，他俯到观察口寻找步兵手势。炮弹打起的碎砖遮住了路牌，枪声从门洞里传来。他用手指在隔板上划出方向，等驾驶员再转一次。\n\n这里发生了首次有记录的坦克对战。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Villers-Bretonneux · 24 April 1918\n\nThe crew assistant climbs away from the engine, his sleeve brushing a hot pipe. The tank turns at the village entrance. He tightens a loose strap as someone knocks on the hull outside.\n\nThe driver cannot see the side alley, so the assistant looks for infantry gestures through a port. Broken brick hides the signpost and firing comes from a doorway. He traces a direction on the partition and waits for another turn.\n\nThe first recorded tank-versus-tank battle took place here.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 一九一八年八月八日\n\n前哨的报告上写着战车，送信的人却说不清邻队在哪里。雾中的田野传来发动机声，路口挤满返回部队。反坦克枪组把器材放下，朝来路寻找射位。\n\n机枪掩护孤立阵位撤出的人，增援在另一侧逆向通过。军士把携弹手叫到残墙下，逐个问前面的情况。一名满身泥土的士兵指向雾里，手仍没有放下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · Eight August nineteen eighteen\n\nThe report names tanks, but its runner cannot place the neighbouring unit. Engines sound across the misty fields. Returning troops crowd the junction. The anti-tank crew lowers its equipment and searches for a position facing the approach.\n\nA machine gun covers men leaving isolated posts while reinforcements pass the other way. The NCO calls bearers under the ruined wall and asks each about the front. One soldier covered in mud points into the mist. His arm stays raised as more men pass.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("一九一八年八月八日，亚眠以东的协约国进攻切断德军前哨之间的通信。雾遮住田野动静，步兵与坦克的报告从前线各处送来。后方道路挤满返回部队，增援仍试图逆向前行。\n\n本连在后卫所需的通路附近交战，机枪与反坦克组聚在路口，掩护离开孤立阵位的人。有些哨位仍在视线之外抵抗，炮击破坏和协约国压力威胁着撤离与补给共用的道路。各队对邻近地段的掌握并不完整。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("The Allied attack east of Amiens on 8 August 1918 is cutting communications between German forward posts. Mist obscures movement across the fields, while reports of infantry and tanks arrive from different parts of the front. Rear roads fill with withdrawing troops as reinforcements try to move forward.\n\nThe company is engaged around routes needed by the rear guard. Machine gun and anti-tank crews gather near road junctions, covering men coming out of isolated positions. Some posts remain active beyond the company's view. Artillery damage and Allied pressure threaten the passages carrying both the withdrawal and German supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 亚眠以东 · 1918年8月8日\n\n传令兵在雾里找到约定的矮墙，墙后却只剩一只翻倒的电话。他把纸袋贴在胸前，沿发动机声传来的方向蹲下。路上有部队退回来，没人说清前队在哪里。\n\n新枪位在另一处残墙下，他把命令交给满身泥土的军官。纸上写的路口已经堵满车辆，铅笔便划向旁边的小沟。传令兵收好回执，鞋带断了一头也没有停下。\n\n鲁登道夫称这一天为德国陆军的黑暗之日。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day."), TEXT("WAR LOG · East of Amiens · 8 August 1918\n\nThe runner finds the appointed wall in the fog, with only an overturned telephone behind it. He holds his envelope close and crouches towards the engine noise. Retreating men cannot locate the leading troops.\n\nAt another wall he gives the order to a mud-covered officer. Vehicles fill the junction named on the sheet, so a pencil points to a side ditch. The runner pockets the receipt and leaves with one lace broken.\n\nLudendorff called it the German Army's black day.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 一九一八年八月下旬\n\n旧铁丝横在撤回路上，工兵蹲下把断股搬开。加拿大部队已穿过前方阵位，村边的枪组还在射击。炮火又翻出遗弃弹药，白垩土里露着一枚弹尖。\n\n携弹队与换防人员在田界碰面，伤员从窄路中间送走。军士先让担架过去，再叫后面的人沿沟走。枪手回头找自己的携弹兵，路口已被车辆堵住。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August nineteen eighteen\n\nOld wire crosses the withdrawal route. A pioneer crouches to move the broken strands. Canadian troops have passed the forward works, and guns still fire beside the village. Shellfire exposes abandoned ammunition, leaving a pointed shell in the chalk.\n\nBearers meet reliefs at a field boundary while wounded men pass between them. The NCO lets a stretcher through first, then directs the others along the ditch. A gunner turns to find his bearer, but vehicles have blocked the junction behind the position.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("一九一八年八月下旬，斯卡尔普沿线德军后卫面对协约国在白垩地带的再次推进。加拿大部队越过旧阵位，接近后方村落与道路。早先铁丝和遗弃弹药如今也挡住德军撤回路线。\n\n本连在这些旧工事周围掩护后方交通，工兵查看障碍，机枪组占住接近地段。受损田界提供遮蔽，却藏着未爆弹并打断行进。弹药、换防队和伤员仍从这里经过，协约国压力正在传到相邻地段，道路逐渐拥挤。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("In late August 1918, German rear guards along the Scarpe face a renewed Allied advance through the chalk country. Canadian troops are crossing old positions towards villages and roads behind the line. Earlier wire and discarded ammunition now obstruct routes also needed by withdrawing German units.\n\nThe company covers part of the rearward traffic through these former works. Engineers examine obstacles while machine gun crews occupy positions near the approaches. Damaged field boundaries provide cover but conceal unexploded shells and interrupt movement. Ammunition, reliefs and wounded men continue to pass as Allied pressure reaches the neighbouring sectors.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 斯卡尔普 · 1918年8月下旬\n\n葬埋兵从白垩里取出一块姓名牌，把它擦净放进布袋。旧铁丝横过撤回路，旁边的铲柄已经裂开。他换到较软的地面，先让过经过的炮车。\n\n村口枪声没有停，另一名士兵送来一张位置草图。他把新土旁的木桩扶直，在纸上记下田界。撤离口令从路上传来，他捡起断铲，袋口仍用手按着。\n\n协约国在百日攻势中持续迫使德军后撤。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Scarpe · Late August 1918\n\nThe burial detail recovers a name tag from the chalk and wipes it clean for a cloth bag. Old wire crosses the withdrawal route. With a split spade handle, he waits for a gun wagon to pass.\n\nFiring continues at the village as another man brings a location sketch. He straightens a stake beside the fresh earth and marks the field boundary. The withdrawal order comes down the road; he gathers the broken spade and closes the bag.\n\nAllied attacks drove the Germans back during the Hundred Days.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 一九一八年九月二十九日\n\n纤道上落满碎土，送弹队要从这里到达岸上枪位。烟把对面坡脚遮住，英军正在接近运河。工兵沿受损岸路查看，枪手俯身从高处寻找水边的动静。\n\n预备队在前哨后等候，换防人员带回道路被打断的消息。军士让两个人抬起一只弹箱，改从斜坡接近。枪声没有停，纤道尽头却已看不到联络兵。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · Twenty-nine September nineteen eighteen\n\nLoose earth covers the towpath carrying ammunition to the guns above. Smoke hides the opposite slope as British troops approach the canal. Pioneers examine the damaged bank route. A gunner bends over his position to watch the water below.\n\nReserves wait behind the posts. Returning reliefs report a break in the path. The NCO has two men lift a box and take it towards the slope instead. The guns continue firing, but the runner at the far end of the towpath is gone.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on twenty-nine September.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("一九一八年九月二十九日，里克瓦尔附近的德军运河阵地遭到英军攻击，协约国也向北面的隧道地段推进。圣康坦运河形成深障碍，纤道和受损岸路联系守军哨位，烟遮住对岸移动。\n\n本连守着一段运河接近线，枪组从岸上射击，工兵照看剩余通路，预备队聚在前哨后。换防与弹药依靠同样狭路。土坡或纤道损坏时，即使武器仍能开火，阵位之间也可能失去联系，后方人员难以靠近。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("On 29 September 1918, the German canal positions near Riqueval face a British attack while Allied forces also advance around the tunnel sector to the north. The St Quentin Canal forms a deep obstacle, with towpaths and damaged bank routes connecting the defending posts. Smoke obscures movement across the water.\n\nThe company defends part of the canal approaches. Gun crews maintain fire from the banks, engineers tend the remaining passages, and reserves assemble behind the forward positions. Reliefs and ammunition depend on the same narrow routes. Damage along a slope or towpath can separate posts even before their weapons are silenced.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 里克瓦尔 · 1918年9月29日\n\n船工把长篙靠在运河墙上，先摸过破船里的漏口。纤道上全是刚落下的碎土，岸边的枪手催他靠近一点。他用旧布堵住裂缝，让船沿绳慢慢移过去。\n\n预备队在高岸后等候，弹箱从坡上滑到船边。船工扶稳船沿，叫他们把重量分到两端。对岸起烟时，他收回长篙，水面上只剩船底带出的一道浑痕。\n\n英军于九月二十九日越过圣康坦运河。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Riqueval · 29 September 1918\n\nThe boatman rests his pole against the canal wall and feels for the leak in a damaged boat. Fresh earth covers the towpath. He plugs the crack with cloth and draws the boat along a rope.\n\nReserves wait behind the high bank while boxes slide towards the boat. He steadies the gunwale and spreads the load between both ends. Smoke rises opposite; the pole comes aboard, leaving a muddy line in the water.\n\nBritish troops crossed the St Quentin Canal on 29 September.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 一九一八年十月\n\n车站还在装运，切口里的列车向谷口开火。公路上有部队撤过来，炮弹落在路堤另一面。守着接近路的步枪手回头，看见携弹兵正从车站跑来。\n\n换防队沿河岸进入阵地，军士把来路交代给新枪手。路堤遮住列车侧面，只露出上面的枪位。车站方向又响起装车声，担架队等着前面的车辆先走。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October nineteen eighteen\n\nLoading continues at the station. The train in the cutting fires towards the valley entrance as troops withdraw along the road. Shells fall beyond the embankment. Riflemen covering the approach turn to see bearers coming from the station.\n\nReliefs enter along the riverbank. The NCO explains the approach to a new gunner. The embankment hides the train's side, leaving its upper guns visible. More loading can be heard behind them. The stretcher party waits for the vehicles ahead to move out.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October nineteen eighteen.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("一九一八年十月，塞勒河谷的德军后卫在协约国压力下掩护部队和物资撤离。渡口与铁路路堤限制后路，车站仍在装车，炮火搜索河谷道路和切口。撤出的交通尚未全部通过。\n\n本连所在的地段有武装列车从铁路切口支援撤运，步兵占据旁边接近路，河岸与路堤遮住部分车辆侧翼。携弹兵和换防队往返车站与前哨之间。协约国进攻进入谷地时，河岸公路仍然拥挤，各处枪组继续照看来路。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("In October 1918, German rear guards in the Selle valley are protecting the withdrawal of troops and stores under Allied pressure. River crossings and railway embankments restrict the routes to the rear. Loading continues at the station while artillery searches the roads and cuttings.\n\nThe company's sector includes an armed train covering evacuation from the railway cutting. Infantry occupy the approaches beside it, where banks and embankments conceal parts of the train's flanks. Ammunition bearers and reliefs pass between the station and forward posts. The river roads remain crowded as the Allied attack reaches the valley.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 塞勒河谷 · 1918年10月\n\n信号兵从车站拿出提灯，灯罩的一面已经碎了。列车在切口里向谷口开火，调车轨旁还堆着未装走的木箱。他站到路堤边，把灯口转向司机。\n\n退下来的部队从轨道上经过，司机暂时看不见手势。信号兵把灯举高，等最后一队走出道岔。车轮响过损坏接头时，他又放低灯口，照着下一根枕木。\n\n塞勒河进攻发生于一九一八年十月。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Selle Valley · October 1918\n\nThe signalman takes a lamp from the station, one pane broken. A train fires along the valley from the cutting. Boxes remain by the siding as he turns the light towards its driver.\n\nRetreating troops cross the rails and hide his signal. He raises the lamp until the last party clears the points. Wheels strike a damaged joint; he lowers the light again to show the next sleeper.\n\nThe Battle of the Selle was fought in October 1918.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 一九一八年十一月初\n\n枪组身旁经过一辆平民手推车，车轮在碎砖上颠簸。加拿大部队正向外围逼近，后卫还守着出口。换防人员沿果园过来，其他部队从残墙后退向城外。\n\n路上挤着伤员和军车，军士不断示意前面继续走。步枪手伏在浅沟里等候，墙另一侧有射击声。手推车卡在一块砖上，旁边的人伸手扶了一把。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November nineteen eighteen\n\nA civilian handcart passes the gun, its wheels jolting over broken bricks. Canadian troops approach the outskirts while the rearguard holds the exit. Reliefs come through the orchard and other parties withdraw beyond the ruined walls.\n\nWounded men and military vehicles fill the road. The NCO keeps signalling those ahead to move. Riflemen wait in a shallow ditch, hearing shots beyond the wall. The handcart catches on a brick beside them; a passing man reaches over to steady its loaded frame.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月初，加拿大部队逼近瓦朗谢讷，德军从城镇接近地段后撤。枪位照看外围公路和出口，城内仍有平民，手推车、军车与伤员一起经过城郊。各条道路的交通仍在继续。\n\n本连担任这里的后卫，换防人员接近枪组，其他部队则从断墙和果园之间向后移动。短促接近线限制观察，加拿大部队对邻近阵位的压力威胁着撤退纵队与补给所需路线。居民区旁的残墙还遮住了部分前方动静。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("At the beginning of November 1918, Canadian troops are advancing towards Valenciennes as German forces withdraw through the town's approaches. Gun positions cover the outer roads and exits. Civilians remain in the settlement, and carts, military vehicles and wounded men share the traffic moving through the outskirts.\n\nThe company serves in this rear guard. Relief parties approach the guns while other troops move towards the rear, passing between broken walls and orchards. Observation is limited across the short approaches. Canadian pressure on nearby positions threatens routes still needed by the withdrawing columns and their supplies.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 瓦朗谢讷外围 · 1918年11月初\n\n押送兵让俘虏贴着路边走，腾出中间给载满伤员的车。瓦朗谢讷外围还在射击，一名俘虏扶着另一人的胳膊。押送兵压低枪口，先去推开卡住的车轮。\n\n居民的手推车从果园里出来，双方都在碎砖前停了一下。他用手指向较平的沟边，让队伍逐人过去。俘虏回头看城里，押送兵拍了拍身旁的立柱，催后队跟上。\n\n加拿大部队于十一月初攻占瓦朗谢讷。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Outside Valenciennes · Early November 1918\n\nThe escort keeps prisoners beside the road to leave room for a casualty wagon. Firing continues outside Valenciennes. One prisoner supports another; the escort lowers his rifle to help free the wheel.\n\nA civilian handcart emerges from the orchard and both parties stop at the rubble. He points towards the smoother ditch edge and sends them through one by one. A prisoner looks back at the town; the escort calls the rear party forward.\n\nCanadian troops took Valenciennes in early November.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n药务兵在路口打开铁盒，瓶身上的纸签已经湿透。后卫仍向桑布尔渡口射击，空药瓶随着车轮震动轻轻相碰。他把干布铺在箱底，重新放好剩下的药。\n\n一个士兵来领包扎布，递上的手掌还沾着枪油。药务兵把整卷布交给他，将空盒系回车旁。居民与军车开始往后走，他在车板上坐稳，留出一只手抓住缰绳。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe medical orderly opens a tin at the junction, its bottle labels soaked. The rearguard still fires towards the Sambre crossing. Empty bottles knock together as he lines the box with dry cloth.\n\nA soldier comes for dressings with gun oil on his palm. The orderly hands him a whole roll and ties the empty tin to the cart. Civilians and wagons begin moving back; he settles on the board with a hand free for the reins.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 一九一八年十一月四日\n\n后卫机枪朝着运河渡口，预备队留在路口等人。别处停战的消息到了，今天的撤离命令也到了。城郊公路上，居民推着家当夹在撤回的纵队之间。\n\n前哨还有人员没有回来，携弹兵把剩余箱子放在墙下。军士望着来路，示意最后一队先通过障碍。枪手握住已经发热的握把，河岸那边又传来步枪声。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n药务兵在路口打开铁盒，瓶身上的纸签已经湿透。后卫仍向桑布尔渡口射击，空药瓶随着车轮震动轻轻相碰。他把干布铺在箱底，重新放好剩下的药。\n\n一个士兵来领包扎布，递上的手掌还沾着枪油。药务兵把整卷布交给他，将空盒系回车旁。居民与军车开始往后走，他在车板上坐稳，留出一只手抓住缰绳。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe medical orderly opens a tin at the junction, its bottle labels soaked. The rearguard still fires towards the Sambre crossing. Empty bottles knock together as he lines the box with dry cloth.\n\nA soldier comes for dressings with gun oil on his palm. The orderly hands him a whole roll and ties the empty tin to the cart. Civilians and wagons begin moving back; he settles on the board with a hand free for the reins.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · Four November nineteen eighteen\n\nThe rearguard gun faces the canal crossing. Reserves wait at the junction for men still forward. News of armistices elsewhere has arrived with today's withdrawal orders. Civilians push their belongings between the returning columns on the outskirts road.\n\nSome men remain at the outposts. Bearers put their last boxes under a wall. The NCO watches the approach and signals another party through the damaged obstacles. The gunner holds the warm grips. Rifle fire sounds again from the bank beyond the crossing.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at eleven on eleven November.")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n药务兵在路口打开铁盒，瓶身上的纸签已经湿透。后卫仍向桑布尔渡口射击，空药瓶随着车轮震动轻轻相碰。他把干布铺在箱底，重新放好剩下的药。\n\n一个士兵来领包扎布，递上的手掌还沾着枪油。药务兵把整卷布交给他，将空盒系回车旁。居民与军车开始往后走，他在车板上坐稳，留出一只手抓住缰绳。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe medical orderly opens a tin at the junction, its bottle labels soaked. The rearguard still fires towards the Sambre crossing. Empty bottles knock together as he lines the box with dry cloth.\n\nA soldier comes for dressings with gun oil on his palm. The orderly hands him a whole roll and ties the empty tin to the cart. Civilians and wagons begin moving back; he settles on the board with a hand free for the reins.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("一九一八年十一月四日，其他战场停战的消息到了德军后方，西线仍在交战。协约国接近桑布尔渡口与附近居民区，新西兰部队在另一段战线逼近勒凯努瓦，德军纵队继续后撤。\n\n本连在运河接近地段掩护一条局部退路。机枪组守望渡口，预备队等待从前哨返回的人员。平民和军队共用城郊公路，受损障碍与协约国压力拖慢通行。后卫仍依靠这些狭路接应未撤出的部队，并运走剩余物资。")},
    {TEXT("战时日志 · 桑布尔接近地 · 1918年11月4日\n\n药务兵在路口打开铁盒，瓶身上的纸签已经湿透。后卫仍向桑布尔渡口射击，空药瓶随着车轮震动轻轻相碰。他把干布铺在箱底，重新放好剩下的药。\n\n一个士兵来领包扎布，递上的手掌还沾着枪油。药务兵把整卷布交给他，将空盒系回车旁。居民与军车开始往后走，他在车板上坐稳，留出一只手抓住缰绳。\n\n十一月十一日十一时，西线停战生效。"), TEXT("WAR LOG · Sambre Approaches · 4 November 1918\n\nThe medical orderly opens a tin at the junction, its bottle labels soaked. The rearguard still fires towards the Sambre crossing. Empty bottles knock together as he lines the box with dry cloth.\n\nA soldier comes for dressings with gun oil on his palm. The orderly hands him a whole roll and ties the empty tin to the cart. Civilians and wagons begin moving back; he settles on the board with a hand free for the reins.\n\nThe Western Front armistice took effect at 11 a.m. on 11 November."), TEXT("By 4 November 1918, news of armistices in other theatres has reached the German rear, but the Western Front continues fighting. Allied troops are approaching the Sambre crossings and nearby settlements. Elsewhere along the front, New Zealand forces are nearing Le Quesnoy as German columns move back.\n\nThe company covers a local withdrawal route beside the canal approaches. Machine gun crews watch the crossings, and reserves wait for parties returning from forward posts. Civilian and military traffic share the roads through the outskirts. Damaged obstacles and Allied pressure slow movement along passages still needed by the German rear guard.")},
