    {TEXT("他的第二集团军参加了 1917 年康布雷反击与 1918 年春的米夏埃尔攻势。到亚眠，进攻者转为守军，面对协约国炮兵、坦克与步兵的协同突击。"), TEXT("His Second Army fought in the Cambrai counterattack of 1917 and the Michael offensive in spring 1918. At Amiens, the attackers had become defenders, facing coordinated Allied artillery, tanks and infantry."), TEXT("His Second Army fought in the Cambrai counterattack of 1917 and the Michael offensive in spring 1918. At Amiens, the attackers had become defenders, facing coordinated Allied artillery, tanks and infantry.")},
    {TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。"), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads."), TEXT("第一集团军司令。八月二十六日，他的部队以加拿大军为先导，在斯卡尔普河与桑塞河掩护的翼侧向东推进。眼前的任务是越过旧阵地，让炮兵与补给跟上持续变化的战线。")},
    {TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。"), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads."), TEXT("Commander of First Army. On 26 August his troops advanced east with the Canadian Corps in the lead and their flanks protected by the Scarpe and Sensee rivers. The task was to cross old positions while bringing guns and supplies up behind the moving front.")},
    {TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。"), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads."), TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。")},
    {TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。"), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads."), TEXT("On twenty-six August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads.")},
    {TEXT("八月二十六日，他的第一集团军以加拿大军展开斯卡尔普攻势。部队越过旧阵地向东推进；炮兵与补给仍要沿破损道路跟进。"), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads."), TEXT("On 26 August, the Canadian Corps of his First Army opened the Scarpe attack. Troops advanced east through the old positions; guns and supplies still had to follow over damaged roads.")},
    {TEXT("第四集团军从亚眠推进到兴登堡防线。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战；深切的运河渡口需要炮兵、步兵与工兵协同。防线终于被打开。"), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens to the Hindenburg Line. Australians and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt; the deeply cut canal demanded cooperation between guns, infantry and engineers. The line was eventually broken."), TEXT("第四集团军由亚眠继续向兴登堡防线推进。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战，其他渡口同样需要炮火、步兵与工兵配合；运河的深切地形让每一条通路都至关重要。")},
    {TEXT("第四集团军从亚眠推进到兴登堡防线。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战；深切的运河渡口需要炮兵、步兵与工兵协同。防线终于被打开。"), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens to the Hindenburg Line. Australians and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt; the deeply cut canal demanded cooperation between guns, infantry and engineers. The line was eventually broken."), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens towards the Hindenburg Line. Australian and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt, while other crossings also demanded close cooperation between gunners, infantry and pioneers. The deep canal cutting made every approach vital.")},
    {TEXT("第四集团军从亚眠推进到兴登堡防线。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战；深切的运河渡口需要炮兵、步兵与工兵协同。防线终于被打开。"), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens to the Hindenburg Line. Australians and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt; the deeply cut canal demanded cooperation between guns, infantry and engineers. The line was eventually broken."), TEXT("第四集团军从亚眠推进到兴登堡防线。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战；深切的运河渡口需要炮兵、步兵与工兵协同。防线终于被打开。")},
    {TEXT("第四集团军从亚眠推进到兴登堡防线。澳大利亚与配属美军在贝利库尔作战；深切的运河渡口需要炮兵、步兵与工兵协同。防线终于被打开。"), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens to the Hindenburg Line. Australians and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt; the deeply cut canal demanded cooperation between guns, infantry and engineers. The line was eventually broken."), TEXT("Fourth Army advanced from Amiens to the Hindenburg Line. Australians and attached American troops fought at Bellicourt; the deeply cut canal demanded cooperation between guns, infantry and engineers. The line was eventually broken.")},
    {TEXT("突破兴登堡防线后，他率第四集团军追到塞勒河。桥头、村落和道路重新成为争夺目标；炮兵与邻军保持联络，部队继续越过河谷向东推进。"), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, he led Fourth Army to the Selle. Bridgeheads, villages and roads became the next objectives. Keeping touch with artillery and neighbouring formations, his troops continued east across the river valley."), TEXT("突破兴登堡防线之后，第四集团军继续追击到塞勒河。曾经依托连续战壕的战争再次转入河谷与村落，桥头、道路和邻军联络决定了推进能否持续。")},
    {TEXT("突破兴登堡防线后，他率第四集团军追到塞勒河。桥头、村落和道路重新成为争夺目标；炮兵与邻军保持联络，部队继续越过河谷向东推进。"), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, he led Fourth Army to the Selle. Bridgeheads, villages and roads became the next objectives. Keeping touch with artillery and neighbouring formations, his troops continued east across the river valley."), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, Fourth Army pursued the enemy to the Selle. The war moved from continuous trench systems into valleys and villages. Bridgeheads, roads and contact with neighbouring formations determined whether the advance could continue.")},
    {TEXT("突破兴登堡防线后，他率第四集团军追到塞勒河。桥头、村落和道路重新成为争夺目标；炮兵与邻军保持联络，部队继续越过河谷向东推进。"), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, he led Fourth Army to the Selle. Bridgeheads, villages and roads became the next objectives. Keeping touch with artillery and neighbouring formations, his troops continued east across the river valley."), TEXT("突破兴登堡防线后，他率第四集团军追到塞勒河。桥头、村落和道路重新成为争夺目标；炮兵与邻军保持联络，部队继续越过河谷向东推进。")},
    {TEXT("突破兴登堡防线后，他率第四集团军追到塞勒河。桥头、村落和道路重新成为争夺目标；炮兵与邻军保持联络，部队继续越过河谷向东推进。"), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, he led Fourth Army to the Selle. Bridgeheads, villages and roads became the next objectives. Keeping touch with artillery and neighbouring formations, his troops continued east across the river valley."), TEXT("After breaking the Hindenburg Line, he led Fourth Army to the Selle. Bridgeheads, villages and roads became the next objectives. Keeping touch with artillery and neighbouring formations, his troops continued east across the river valley.")},
    {TEXT("百日攻势中，他率第三集团军继续向东，新西兰师亦在其列。勒凯努瓦城墙与桑布尔村落仍有守军；停战前的最后一周，前线继续交战。"), TEXT("During the Hundred Days, his Third Army continued east with the New Zealand Division in its ranks. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages were still defended. Fighting continued through the final week before the armistice."), TEXT("第三集团军在百日攻势中继续向东推进，新西兰师也在其序列内。勒凯努瓦的城墙与桑布尔战区的村落仍有守军；停战以前的最后一周，前线的任务并没有因胜利将近而变得轻松。")},
    {TEXT("百日攻势中，他率第三集团军继续向东，新西兰师亦在其列。勒凯努瓦城墙与桑布尔村落仍有守军；停战前的最后一周，前线继续交战。"), TEXT("During the Hundred Days, his Third Army continued east with the New Zealand Division in its ranks. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages were still defended. Fighting continued through the final week before the armistice."), TEXT("Third Army continued east during the Hundred Days, with the New Zealand Division among its formations. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages still held defenders. The last week before the armistice brought no easy duty at the front.")},
    {TEXT("百日攻势中，他率第三集团军继续向东，新西兰师亦在其列。勒凯努瓦城墙与桑布尔村落仍有守军；停战前的最后一周，前线继续交战。"), TEXT("During the Hundred Days, his Third Army continued east with the New Zealand Division in its ranks. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages were still defended. Fighting continued through the final week before the armistice."), TEXT("百日攻势中，他率第三集团军继续向东，新西兰师亦在其列。勒凯努瓦城墙与桑布尔村落仍有守军；停战前的最后一周，前线继续交战。")},
    {TEXT("百日攻势中，他率第三集团军继续向东，新西兰师亦在其列。勒凯努瓦城墙与桑布尔村落仍有守军；停战前的最后一周，前线继续交战。"), TEXT("During the Hundred Days, his Third Army continued east with the New Zealand Division in its ranks. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages were still defended. Fighting continued through the final week before the armistice."), TEXT("During the Hundred Days, his Third Army continued east with the New Zealand Division in its ranks. Le Quesnoy's walls and the Sambre villages were still defended. Fighting continued through the final week before the armistice.")},
    {TEXT("他历经东线、马其顿与意大利战场，二月起执掌第十七集团军。春季攻势转为夏末防御；斯卡尔普方向的旧阵地与后卫未能使战线停止后移。"), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took Seventeenth Army in February. Spring offensives gave way to late-summer defence. Old positions and rearguards on the Scarpe could delay the retreat, but could not stop it."), TEXT("先后经历东线、马其顿和意大利战场，二月起接掌第十七集团军。春季的进攻已转为夏末的防御，他的部队需要用旧阵地和后卫争取时间，抵挡斯卡尔普方向的持续压力。")},
    {TEXT("他历经东线、马其顿与意大利战场，二月起执掌第十七集团军。春季攻势转为夏末防御；斯卡尔普方向的旧阵地与后卫未能使战线停止后移。"), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took Seventeenth Army in February. Spring offensives gave way to late-summer defence. Old positions and rearguards on the Scarpe could delay the retreat, but could not stop it."), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took command of Seventeenth Army in February. Spring's offensive had become late summer's defence. Old positions and rearguards had to buy time against sustained pressure along the Scarpe.")},
    {TEXT("他历经东线、马其顿与意大利战场，二月起执掌第十七集团军。春季攻势转为夏末防御；斯卡尔普方向的旧阵地与后卫未能使战线停止后移。"), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took Seventeenth Army in February. Spring offensives gave way to late-summer defence. Old positions and rearguards on the Scarpe could delay the retreat, but could not stop it."), TEXT("他历经东线、马其顿与意大利战场，二月起执掌第十七集团军。春季攻势转为夏末防御；斯卡尔普方向的旧阵地与后卫未能使战线停止后移。")},
    {TEXT("他历经东线、马其顿与意大利战场，二月起执掌第十七集团军。春季攻势转为夏末防御；斯卡尔普方向的旧阵地与后卫未能使战线停止后移。"), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took Seventeenth Army in February. Spring offensives gave way to late-summer defence. Old positions and rearguards on the Scarpe could delay the retreat, but could not stop it."), TEXT("After service on the Eastern, Macedonian and Italian fronts, he took Seventeenth Army in February. Spring offensives gave way to late-summer defence. Old positions and rearguards on the Scarpe could delay the retreat, but could not stop it.")},
    {TEXT("这位萨克森前战争大臣曾指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，协约国军正攻向兴登堡防线。分散据点仍需相互支援，防线却已难守。"), TEXT("The former Saxon war minister had commanded corps before taking Second Army in late September. Allied forces were attacking the Hindenburg Line. Its scattered strongpoints still depended on mutual support, but the line could no longer hold."), TEXT("萨克森军人，曾任王国战争大臣并指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，兴登堡防线正面临协约军的新一轮攻势；他的职责是让分散的支点继续构成能够互相支援的防御。")},
    {TEXT("这位萨克森前战争大臣曾指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，协约国军正攻向兴登堡防线。分散据点仍需相互支援，防线却已难守。"), TEXT("The former Saxon war minister had commanded corps before taking Second Army in late September. Allied forces were attacking the Hindenburg Line. Its scattered strongpoints still depended on mutual support, but the line could no longer hold."), TEXT("A Saxon officer, former war minister and corps commander. When he took over Second Army in late September, the Hindenburg Line faced another Allied offensive. His task was to keep scattered strongpoints fighting as a mutually supporting defence.")},
    {TEXT("这位萨克森前战争大臣曾指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，协约国军正攻向兴登堡防线。分散据点仍需相互支援，防线却已难守。"), TEXT("The former Saxon war minister had commanded corps before taking Second Army in late September. Allied forces were attacking the Hindenburg Line. Its scattered strongpoints still depended on mutual support, but the line could no longer hold."), TEXT("这位萨克森前战争大臣曾指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，协约国军正攻向兴登堡防线。分散据点仍需相互支援，防线却已难守。")},
    {TEXT("这位萨克森前战争大臣曾指挥军级部队。九月下旬接掌第二集团军时，协约国军正攻向兴登堡防线。分散据点仍需相互支援，防线却已难守。"), TEXT("The former Saxon war minister had commanded corps before taking Second Army in late September. Allied forces were attacking the Hindenburg Line. Its scattered strongpoints still depended on mutual support, but the line could no longer hold."), TEXT("The former Saxon war minister had commanded corps before taking Second Army in late September. Allied forces were attacking the Hindenburg Line. Its scattered strongpoints still depended on mutual support, but the line could no longer hold.")},
    {TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。"), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued."), TEXT("第二集团军在持续后撤中寻找新的立足点。河流和铁路可以帮助后卫争取时间，却无法替代步兵守住通路；从纵深防线到河谷阵地，保存联络已和保存兵力同样困难。")},
    {TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。"), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued."), TEXT("Second Army sought fresh footholds during its continuing retreat. Rivers and railways could buy the rearguards time but could not replace infantry on the approaches. Maintaining communications was becoming as difficult as preserving manpower.")},
    {TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。"), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued."), TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。")},
    {TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。"), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued."), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways. Rearguards bought time while infantry held the approaches. After leaving the defences in depth for the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued.")},
    {TEXT("第二集团军沿河流和铁路后撤，后卫争取时间，步兵守住通路。从纵深防线退到河谷之后，维持部队联络与保存兵力同样困难。撤退仍在继续。"), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued."), TEXT("Second Army fell back along rivers and railways, with rearguards holding the approaches. In the river valleys, keeping units in touch was as difficult as preserving their strength. The retreat continued.")},
    {TEXT("工兵出身的他长期从事要塞事务，曾在阿尔贡作战。十月十二日接掌第十七集团军后，部队仍在后撤；河岸、村落与有限道路成了后卫的依托。"), TEXT("An engineer officer experienced in fortifications, he had commanded in the Argonne. After taking Seventeenth Army on 12 October, he faced a retreating front. Riverbanks, villages and the few available roads became positions for his rearguards."), TEXT("工兵出身，长期从事工程兵与要塞事务，曾在阿尔贡指挥作战。十月十二日接掌第十七集团军之后，他面对的是不断后移的战线；河岸、村落与有限的交通线成为最后的后卫依托。")},
    {TEXT("工兵出身的他长期从事要塞事务，曾在阿尔贡作战。十月十二日接掌第十七集团军后，部队仍在后撤；河岸、村落与有限道路成了后卫的依托。"), TEXT("An engineer officer experienced in fortifications, he had commanded in the Argonne. After taking Seventeenth Army on 12 October, he faced a retreating front. Riverbanks, villages and the few available roads became positions for his rearguards."), TEXT("An engineer officer with long experience of fortifications and earlier command in the Argonne. After taking over Seventeenth Army on 12 October, he faced a steadily receding front. Riverbanks, villages and limited roads became the last rearguard positions.")},
